0] verbatim; \"every frame in the primary classfile method-name set\" = set inclusion; missing =\n97\t  `none`/`false`. Primary classfile (d07 and d26) = the manifest Main-Class, never a `$_main_closure1`; method_count = ALL\n98\t  method_info rows incl. Groovy synthetics (10). Inner class names keep `Variant000` although basenames say `sample`.\n99\t- **Member basename vocabulary (D22)** -- `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`; group by `dNN--` + extension/role tag only.\n100\t- **Primary vs support members (D3, D22, D23)** -- primary assembly + `.runtimeconfig.json` (+ D22 `FSharp.Core.dll`); question:\n101\t  \"primary managed assembly ... runtimeconfig and dependency DLL members are delivery support only\". Primary = the `.dll` whose\n102\t  name is not a framework/dependency (FSharp.Core, System.*, Microsoft.*), i.e. the one carrying HCFG; hash ALL members.\n103\t- **Stripped carry-over d01** -- re-rolls stripped in some sets (D15-D17 Mastery, D17/D19 TT, D23 Mastery set6): symbols/\n104\t  disassembly `[]`, has_symtab `false`, recover_code `none` (GM-confirmed; leaf-heuristic constants rejected). Pair by sha256.\n105\t- **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` ids (2-12 sets; D27 11 x ~36 MB, D28 12 x ~17 MB), each its own delivery; each set's 1st question ends `Evidence\n106\t  case: dNN-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]` (TT `dNN-tt-...`) = set->delivery map. Per-member caches key on\n107\t  (delivery, member name) or sha256, never `id(bytes)` (D25: 5/9 sets cross-wired, see Pitfalls).\n108\t- **kind / field sets per group** -- `elf_class`/`machine` exact_text on d01 but INTEGER (`64`/`62`) on d08/d15/d21 (dispatch on\n109\t  `answer_format.kind`, which can change between fetches, D17); `has_<x>` = a structural marker of <x> in THIS member; old groups\n110\t  gain ids over days (D8, D17, D28): answer by field name from THAT member's facts dict.\n111\t- **Backfill #3 spec grammar (D28, 54 ids on d01-d27)** -- every new old-group id spells its rule