s hit the 8 s timeout under load (pyelftools `.symtab` parse ~1 s/set) -> struct-parsed symtab reader, ~1 s/set total.\n202\t\n203\t## GM answer conventions learned\n204\t| Field family | Accepted form | Rejected (never resubmit) |\n205\t|---|---|---|\n206\t| elf_class | exact_text: `ELF64`/`ELF32` (readelf style); `kind: integer` (D8+): the bit width `64`/`32` | ELFCLASS64; `2`/`1` |\n207\t| machine (`kind: integer`, D8-D9, D15, D21 loader/plugin, D27 gcc/tcc) | decimal e_machine (`62` = x86-64), also for an ET_DYN `.cmxs`; same for every compiler of one source | — |\n208\t| endianness | `little` / `big` | little endian, lsb, msb |\n209\t| machine (ELF) | `x86-64`, `x86`, `AArch64`, `ARM` (D19 text: tool labels and decimal/hex codes also accepted) | EM_X86_64, x86_64, amd64 (pre-D17 exact_text) |\n210\t| machine (PE FILE_HEADER) | 0x14c → `i386`; 0x8664 → `x86-64` | x86 (for PE i386); raw `0x8664` |\n211\t| architecture | the same machine words (Go amd64 → `x86-64`) | amd64, arm64, 386, x86_64 |\n212\t| elf_type | `ET_EXEC` / `ET_DYN` | EXEC |\n213\t| entry_point, crc32_hex, xor_key_hex | lowercase hex with `0x` (crc `0x%08x`, key `0x%02x`) | — |\n214\t| recover_code (`kind: integer`) | base-10 integer (`mov eax, 0x1fa4` → 8100); `none` if the symbol is absent (stripped d01) | the stripped/renamed leaf's constant (8114, 8106) |\n215\t| has_symtab / has_cpp_* / has_go_runtime / has_rust_mangled_symbol / has_coroutine_runtime | enum `true`/`false` | — |\n216\t| marker | exact `.huntress` string without the NUL; `none` if the section is missing | — |\n217\t| format (enum since D17-D19 on d12+) | `elf`, `pe`, `pe_cli` (.NET), `jar`, `wasm`, `neko_bytecode` (listed, unseen) | ELF, ELF64, elf64-x86-64, exe, pe32+, jar_jvm, ~50 .NET synonyms |\n218\t| format / arch per container (language/compiler never changes the label) | compiled ELF (D8-D21, D27 V via gcc AND tcc) `elf`/`x86-64`; WASM `wasm`/`wasm32`; .NET any language (C#, F#, VB.NET) `pe_cli`/`i386`; any JVM jar (Ja