(same size + 28-entry section table; a vs b = 1 differing byte, the role string in .rodata; false friend ~2k bytes from .text on, own HCFG). Only routing was asked; a D29 sequel will likely ask metrics. Build lib.binary.member_similarity(members) -> {pair: {diff_bytes, first_diff, same_sections:[...], text_sha256_equal, func_hash_overlap, string_jaccard}} + cluster_members(members, rule) where the rule is parsed from the question (equal .text hash / same HCFG JSON / same trace profile / threshold). Functions on stripped ELFs from .eh_frame FDE pc ranges (pyelftools CFI), hash = sha256 of capstone mnemonics+operand kinds (mask imm/disp/rip-rel). Fixtures: the D28 trio from challenges/day28 cases + gcc -O0/-O2 builds of one source and one different source. Expose results via register_generic for ids like `<a>_<b>_diff_bytes`, `family_members`, `false_friend`, `cluster_count`.\"},\n405:  {\"id\": \"toolchain-attribution-verdicts\", \"concept\": \"Toolchain attribution as enum/text answers per member: compiler (gcc/clang/tcc/zig/msvc/mingw/odin/v), compiler version, linker (bfd/gold/lld/mold/tcc/link.exe), libc (glibc/musl/bionic/msvcrt/ucrt), debug format (dwarf2-5/stabs/codeview/none), static vs dynamic, PIE, hash style\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D27 'name the toolchain' was unasked and D28 moved on to family clustering, but a D29 lineage/attribution step or the D31 capstone could ask it on d27/d28. Evidence rules: .comment banner (often stripped), DW_AT_producer (`readelf --debug-dump=info`), .stab/.stabstr (tcc), `.lto_priv`/`.constprop` (gcc LTO), `.note.gnu.gold-version` (gold), `.comment` `Linker: LLD` (lld), `mold` in .comment, tcc unmerged `.text.<fn>` + per-object GNU_PROPERTY notes, PE Rich header comp ids (MSVC) vs MinGW `.CRT`/`__mingw_` symbols, PT_INTERP (ld-musl vs ld-linux), Odin `/odin/base/runtime` paths, V `builtin__`/`_vinit`. Output tokens lowercase; when an enum is supplied pick from it. Fixtures: gcc/clang-18/tcc(if apt)/aarch64-gcc builds of one C file with -g/-s variants + the d27/d28 members.\"},\n407:  {\"id\": \"contract-revision-watch\", \"concept\": \"Organizers revise the live contract mid-day (D17: exact_text -> enum + rule text)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"When an exact_text label resists ~10 probes: write HELP, then re-pull the contract (`hctf status <id>`) every ~20-30 min and diff question text/answer_format per id; D17 the revision converted ~3.5 h and ~10.9k rejected probes into CORRECT within a minute. Never run mass automated label grouptests on a closed-vocabulary GM field.\"},\n410:  {\"id\": \"theme-facts-recording\", \"concept\": \"Record each day's prompt-theme facts during the single solve (asked on its own day since D19, or in a later backfill)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's (overlay_offset/overlay_size, config after unpacking) and D20's (overlay_offset, hcfg_resource_size) WERE and D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (stub/overlay header fields, call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts dict should already expose them as candidate field names (d19: overlay_version, k1/k2 hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256). d20: rs20 version, hcfg_resource_size, scratch_size (35), scratch_sha256, scratch text, image_end, GHC version 9.12.2. d21: loader/plugin NEEDED, plugin exports (caml_plugin_header, caml_globals, camlPlugin_000__entry), Caml2007D002 dynheader unit name Plugin_000, loader dlopen/caml_natdynlink_open imports, trace family ocaml_controlled_dynlink_trace / controlled_library_resolution_only, OCaml 4.02.3. d22: ModuleRef names (libc, kernel32.dll), ImplMap rows (import name, module, MappingFlags Winapi/charset not spec), calling MethodDefs, AssemblyRefs (System.Runtime, FSharp.Core, System.Text.Json, netstandard), FSharp resources, trace family fsharp_managed_native_bridge_trace / effects inert_native_process_id_bridge, HCFG .text @15891 + PE-overlay copy @18432. d23: VB.NET (Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core, StandardModuleAttribute, VB$AnonymousType_0`8), predicates Debugger.get_IsAttached / Stopwatch.StartNew+get_ElapsedTicks / Environment.get_ProcessorCount / GetEnvironmentVariable(HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL) vs workstation/analysis/sandbox, branches success/decoy/failure, analysis_detected, trace vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace / inert_predicate_only, HCFG PE overlay @7680 only. d24: changed method `score(Ljava/lang/String;)I` only (class `Day24<Role>000$`), vulnerable nonEmpty-then-charAt(0) (null -> NullPointerException, CWE-476) vs corrected Option(s).filter(nonEmpty).map(charAt 0).getOrElse(-1), $-class sizes 4660 vs 5628, main identical (host-model lookupswitch decoy 32 / success 49 / failure 27 / default failure 1, then score(\\\"benign\\\") + decodeConfig().length), trace scala_patch_diff_trace / benign_control_and_reversion_only + control_positive. d25: Clojure twins, changed fn `parse-frame` only (class `day25.<role>000$parse_frame`), vulnerable `(nth frame 4)` -> RT.nth(Object,int) IndexOutOfBoundsException on a short frame (CWE-125/129), corrected `(if (< 4 (count frame)) (nth frame 4) -1)`, `-main` gate HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL (workstation) + HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT==\\\"1\\\" -> frame [1 2] vs [1 2 3 4 5], trace clojure_bounds_root_cause_trace / bounded_synthetic_fault_only, HCFG base64 in `<role>000__init.class` (Var encoded-config). D26: the theme WAS asked on its own day again (first since D20): crash_fault_method (trace.json frames[0]) + crash_frames_match_methods (frames subset of primary-class method names), read from a JSON sidecar entry inside the jar. Unasked D26 facts worth exposing for a backfill: trace kind (IllegalStateException), frame count/depth, static call chain stageOne->stageTwo->stageThree, throw site (new+athrow in stageThree), env gates HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL/HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT, trace family groovy_synthetic_crash_trace / bounded_caught_exception_only. D28 (family clustering, asked only as routing): record per member the byte-diff counts vs each sibling, .text/.rodata sha256, HCFG campaign prefix (family BR28- vs false friend FF28-), trace branch/event_count records and `cluster_marker_positive`, role string `huntress-role-<role>` -- the likely D29 backfill/sequel fields.\"},\n414:  {\"id\": \"hare-vala-c3-member-fixtures\", \"concept\": \"Next niche native languages as a new-day member (D29-D31): Hare (QBE backend, static, no libc, `rt.`/`hare.` symbols), C3 (`c3`-mangled `module.func`), Vala/Genie (GObject C: `g_object_new`, `_vala_`/`*_get_type`, NEEDED libglib/libgobject), Cython (`__pyx_` .so), hxcpp (`hx::`), Jakt/Carbon-style transpilers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The language track since D27 picks niche native languages the atlas listed (V, Odin). Prebuild cue strings + language_of() entries and make sure header ids + HCFG scan (raw, base64, appended tail) work on each: Vala/Genie can be built locally if `valac` is apt-installable (`apt-get install valac`), Cython with the venv (`pip download` not needed: write C by hand mimicking `__pyx_` symbols if offline); Hare/C3 likely not installable -> synthesise minimal static ELFs with gcc -nostdlib exposing their symbol shapes (`rt.start_ha`, `hare.main`, `.test_array`) and an appended HCFG to test routing. Record install status per toolchain in detail on failure.\"},\n422:  {\"id\": \"static-stack-unwinder\", \"concept\": \"'Unwind the stack' statically: reconstruct the frame list from captured stack memory + the binary's unwind info, without executing anything\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"RBP-chain walk (saved rbp/ret pairs) over a core PT_LOAD or MDMP MemoryList range; CFI unwinding with pyelftools CallFrameInfo (decoded table: CFA rule + RA offset at a pc) for -fomit-frame-pointer code; PE x64 UNWIND_INFO (UWOP codes) from .pdata/.xdata; AArch64 x29/x30 chain. Output frames innermost-first as (module, symbol, offset) and per-function frame sizes (CFA offset at body). Fixtures: same crasher built -O0 (frame pointers) and -O2 -fomit-frame-pointer, plus a MinGW PE.\"},\n425:  {\"id\": \"trace-symbolization-retrace\", \"concept\": \"Symbolize / de-obfuscate crash frames: ProGuard/R8 mapping.txt retrace, stripped addresses via a symbolized twin or build-id debug file, .NET portable PDB file:line\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Combines the D15 stripped/symbolized pair with D26 traces: frames like `a.a.b(Unknown Source)` + a `mapping.txt` member (`orig.Class -> a.a:` / `    12:15:void method():30:33 -> b` line-range maps, inlined frames expand to several), raw addresses / `bin+0x1136` in a stripped ELF resolved through the symbolized twin (same build-id/.text bytes) or a separate `.debug` file (`.gnu_debuglink` CRC32 / build-id path), .NET portable PDB (BSJB `#Pdb` stream, MethodDebugInformation sequence points) -> file:line. Fixtures: tiny ProGuard-style mapping + obfuscated jar names; D15 fixtures for the native side.\"},\n427:  {\"id\": \"solver-member-cache-identity\", \"concept\": \"Per-member caches in the cumulative solver keyed on id(bytes) cross-wire members once Python reuses a freed object's address (D25 Mastery: 55 ids in 5/9 sets answered with another dNN-- group's facts)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"challenges/day25/binary-out-of-bounds/solver/solve.py keys _SHA/_ZIPS/_ISJAR/_FACTS/_CFG on id(b) (lines ~61-126, 303-317, 692, 872-891); with 9 sets x ~34 members the first daemon POST failed (d23 <- d03 config, d22/d15 <- d10 PE header, d06/d24 <- d16 wasm, d25 vulnerable <- d03 pe_cli). Fix before D26's timed modes: key on (delivery path, member name) or sha256, or hold every member's bytes in a list for the run; add a regression that runs a 9-set Mastery case (cases/variant-mastery-f395c0c5) with HCTF_SOLVER_PARALLEL=0 and =1. Diagnostic rule: a rejected value that is a VALID answer for a different group of the same delivery = routing/cache bug, not a label problem. D26: the fix held -- Mastery 10 sets (3120 ids) and TT CORRECT first try; keep the regression and re-check after any set-count jump.\"},\n442:  {\"id\": \"vulnerability-class-classifier\", \"concept\": \"Name the bug class a fix addresses as a CWE token + snake_case name (null deref 476, OOB read 125 / write 787, off-by-one 193, int overflow 190, signedness 195, format string 134, UAF 416, double free 415, div-by-zero 369, unchecked return 252, TOCTOU 367, command injection 78, SQLi 89, path traversal 22, unsafe deserialization 502)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Rule table over the diff facts of jvm-method-patch-diff-facts / native-function-patch-diff / managed-patch-diff-dotnet: added null guard / Option wrap / ifnull / `test;je` -> CWE-476; added index/length compare before array/charAt/memcpy -> 125/787; `<=`->`<` -> 193; `add`->`add.ovf`/Math.addExact/`__builtin_add_overflow` -> 190; `jl`->`jb` -> 195; printf(user)->printf(\\\"%s\\\",user) -> 134; free+null or use-after-free removal -> 416; divisor check -> 369; Runtime.exec/system/ProcessBuilder argument sanitising -> 78; ObjectInputStream.readObject filter -> 502; path normalise/`..` check -> 22. D24 fixture = CWE-476. Emit `CWE-476` and `null_pointer_dereference`; GM spelling unknown -> watch for an enum with accepted_values and read the question rules. D25 fixture = CWE-125 (unchecked index; CWE-129 also plausible): added `(< idx (count v))` guard before nth.\"},\n466:  {\"id\": \"offset-section-mapper\", \"concept\": \"Map a file offset to its container location: ELF section + segment (name, flags, VA), PE section (name, RVA, VA), Mach-O segment,section, WASM data segment index + memory offset\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"BUILT (prebuild-state ok). Underpins hcfg_storage and the likely next location ids (`hcfg_section`, `hcfg_va`/`hcfg_vaddr`, `hcfg_rva`, `hcfg_segment`, `hcfg_mem_offset`). `lib.binary.locate_offset(data, off)` -> {container, section, section_flags, segment_index, vaddr, rva, wasm_data_index, wasm_mem_offset}; pure struct parsing (no pyelftools exceptions on sstripped files: fall back to program headers). Expected spellings to try first: section name verbatim (`.rodata`), VA as lowercase `0x` hex like entry_point. Tests on cached day08-day17 members (D17 Ada blob at file 207432 in `.rodata`, D14 at 4000 in `.hcfg`, D12 at 82928 in `.data`) and the wasm fixtures.\"},\n== challenges/day30/binary-campaign-trail/\n{\n  \"attempt_id\": \"d9159bed-9d6b-4c93-8c0f-530b0e44d7b1\",\n  \"mode\": \"single_solve\",\n  \"started_at\": \"2026-10-31T01:18:02.467Z\",\n  \"name\": \"⚙️ Campaign Trail\",\n  \"prompt\": \"One binary is a clue; a campaign is a story. Reconstruct the loader, library, and config graph across the whole set and map the operation end to end.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d01_artifact_sha256_1\",\n      \"question\": \"In evidence.zip, Use all d01-- members in ZIP central-directory order. Compute SHA-256 over the exact bytes of member 1, where members are the d01-- members in ZIP central-directory order (1-ba\n{\"ts\": \"20261031T011845Z\", \"attempt\": \"d9159bed-9d6b-4c93-8c0f-530b0e44d7b1\", \"answers\": {\"d01_artifact_sha256_1\": \"a0d3aeddb90dccf579e0262704dc7d7c2828121d8cc988f085de169601737b9b\", \"d01_analysis_elf_class\": \"ELF64\", \"d01_analysis_machine\": \"x86-64\", \"d01_analysis_section_names\": \"[\\\"\\\",\\\".interp\\\",\\\".note.gnu.property\\\",\\\".note.ABI-tag\\\",\\\".hash\\\",\\\".gnu.hash\\\",\\\".dynsym\\\",\\\".dynstr\\\",\\\".gnu.ver\n{\"ts\": \"20261031T011848Z\", \"attempt\": \"d9159bed-9d6b-4c93-8c0f-530b0e44d7b1\", \"answers\": {\"d30_artifact_sha256_1\": \"7df5ce6a3f45d9b723b5968541