{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CxjYbEU72joELXxJcTtvbk","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D28 post-run, 2026-10-28)\n191:## Concept table\n335:## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n396:## Readiness gaps\n`-family-a.elf`, `-family-b.elf` (~22.9 KB each, ELF64 x86-64 ET_DYN PIE, glibc: NEEDED libm/libc/ld-linux-x86-64, STRIPPED: ~20\n`.dynsym` entries, no `.symtab`; Odin cues `/odin/base/runtime/os_specific_linux.odin`, `base/runtime: getrandom failed`;\nidentical 28-entry section table, `.text` 0x1ba1 in all three). family-a vs family-b differ in ONE byte (role string\n`huntress-role-family-<x>` in `.rodata`); the false friend differs in ~2k bytes from `.text` on, has different trace event_counts\n(12/10/8 vs 57/40/35) and its OWN valid HCFG (campaign `FF28-...` vs the family's `BR28-...`). HCFG RAW appended exactly at\ne_shoff+e_shnum*64 in each (D27 rule: scan backward from the end). Trace family `odin_family_cluster_trace`/`behavior_cluster_\nonly` + `cluster_marker_positive`. Prompt: \"These binaries might be related -- or they might just look alike. Cluster them by\nbehavior, watch out for false friends, and sort the family from the strangers.\" 14 new ids: 3 sha256, `<role>_format`/\n`<role>_machine` for false_friend/family_a/family_b (hyphen -> underscore), 4 unqualified config_* = consensus of family-a +\nfamily-b (\"do not use false-friend.elf\"), `false_friend_config_campaign`. Theme asked ONLY through that routing (no similarity\nmetric, cluster label or member-count id). **BACKFILL #3**: every old group padded to 14 ids (54 new, 392 = 28 x 14), each a\nSPEC sentence: public substring predicates (`has_nim/fpc/gnat_runtime`, `has_decoy_branch` Latin-1/UTF-16LE), regex counts over\nnonempty `.symtab` names (`symbol_count`, `d_symbol_count`, `crystal_symbol_count`, `handler_symbol_count`), sorted LF-join\nsha256 (`handler_symbols_sha256`, `method_names_sha256`), `structural_artifact_count` + `structural_ordered_set_sha256`\n(colon-join of member digests), `conditional_branch_opcode_count` (Jcc bytes in `.text`), `cli_runtime` (CLI header 2.5),\n`section_count`, `class_count`/`class_name`, `vtable_symbol`, PK19 `packing_key_1/2_hex`, d20 `overlay_size`, new HCFG keys\n`host_model`/`ipv4`, and the role-member config ids not asked before. The D27 solver answered 361/392; generic fallback + two\nGM corrections (d13 count = `.symtab` only, 771 not 1255; d20 overlay_size = len - rfind(`RS20`), 463 not 19) -> CORRECT T+3:23\nafter 5 rejected batch POSTs; TT 54 s (d10 re-rolled to PE: ELF-worded `section_count` = NumberOfSections 9, live worker) /\nMastery 12 sets (4704 ids, ~17 MB each) CORRECT first POST.\nArc since D18 = one structure/behaviour concept per day: call graph -> packing -> resources/overlays -> shared libraries ->\nmanaged/native bridge -> anti-analysis predicates -> PATCH DIFFING (D24) -> BOUNDS-ERROR ROOT CAUSE (D25) -> CRASH TRIAGE (D26,\nASKED) -> COMPILER ATTRIBUTION (D27, unasked) -> FAMILY CLUSTERING (D28, asked only as routing + consensus over a named subset).\nD27-D28 = an ATTRIBUTION arc (toolchain -> family). D29-D31 (3 days left) most plausible, in order: (1) the arc's next step --\nLINEAGE/VARIANT ordering (\"which build came first / evolved from which\", version deltas), shared-code measures (function-hash\noverlap, fuzzy hashes, imphash/telfhash) or a YARA-style family signature (\"write/evaluate the rule that matches the family but\nnot the stranger\"); 3+ look-alike members with more strangers; (2) BACKFILL #4 to ~15/group re-asking THEMES on old groups\n(d19/d20 header fields started it: packing keys, overlay_size; next: d21 NEEDED/exports, d22 ImplMap, d23 predicates, d24/d25\nchanged method, d26 call chain, d27 producer/debug format, d28 cluster membership) -- all as spec sentences; (3) a capstone on\nD31 mixing themes; (4) a native crash/exploit sequel (least likely now). Language track: 