tes (Debugger/Stopwatch/Environment TypeRefs, env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`) | NEVER run it: asked ids are header + HCFG (static); record the predicate list |\n| Go / Rust | `go version -m f`, `lib.binary.go_buildinfo`/`go_pclntab_funcs`; Rust: header + `HCFG` scan, `rustfilt` |\n| `.jar` (Java/Kotlin/Scala/Clojure/Groovy, `Created-By: Huntress deterministic <Lang> factory`) | unzip, Main-Class, `javap -v -p`; HCFG base64 `ldc` may be in Scala `Foo$`, Clojure `<ns>__init`, Groovy `encodedConfig`; `unzip -l` for NON-class sidecars |\n| Crash artifact (`crash/trace.json`, `core`, `*.dmp`, hs_err, ASan) | `jq . trace.json` (frames innermost-first); native: `readelf -n core` -> RIP -> `addr2line -f -e bin`; capstone the faulting insn |\n| Twin/role members (`-stripped`/`-symbolized`, `-loader`/`-plugin`, `-vulnerable`/`-corrected`, `-gcc`/`-tcc`, `-O0`/`-O3`) | route `<tag>_` ids (tag may be a semantic word: `optimized` = `-O3`); diff if asked: `javap -p -c` / `objdump -d` per symbol + `diff`, `rz-diff -t functions a b` |\n| N look-alikes (`-family-a`/`-family-b`/`-false-friend`) | `cmp -l A B \\| wc -l` per pair (D28 twins 1 byte, stranger ~2k), per-member HCFG (stranger `FF28-`); consensus = NAMED members only |\n| V / Odin / FreeBASIC ELF (`main__main`+`builtin__*`; `/odin/base/runtime/*.odin`; fbc rtlib `dev_scrn_init.c`/`dev_scrn_write.c` FILE syms, `fb_*`) | plain ELF (`elf`/62); HCFG RAW at image_end (`grep -abo HCFG F`), \"scan backward from the end\" |\n| **`NEKO` magic / `.n` members (D30: Haxe 4.3.7 build, strings `std/neko/*.hx`, globals `@classes`/`@Loader`/`@String`; header `NEKO` + u32le nglobals/nfields/codesize)** | format `neko_bytecode`; config record RAW at EOF: `grep -abo 'HGRF\\|HCFG' F`, rfind + crc gate; JSON path from the question (`graph.config.X` -> obj[\"config\"][\"X\"]); `nekoc`/`haxe` only for theme facts |\n| Record magic you have not seen (`HGRF`, next ???) \"uses the same 12-byte layout as HCFG\" | generic 4-byte-magic record decoder: magic\\|ver\\|key\\|u16 len\\|u32 crc\\|xor payload; scan direction + member from the question |\n| Backfill \"Evaluate this public predicate\", \"count names that match /re/\", \"sort ... SHA-256\" | `lib.binary.generic_field(blob, suffix, question, member)`; `.symtab` only (`.dynsym` if none) |\n| Same-source builds named by COMPILER or FLAGS, \"name the toolchain\", \"account for every optimization\" | header + consensus HCFG (asked D27/D29). Facts if asked: `readelf --debug-dump=info F \\| grep -m2 producer`, `.comment`, gcc IPA suffixes, tcc `.stab`, PT_INTERP libc; O-level: function count/inlining, `.text` size |\n| Swift ELF (`swift5_*`, 60+ MB) | never eager-parse symbols; regex `SENGR` base64 in `.rodata`; `bin/swift-demangle` |\n| Nim / D / Crystal / FPC / ObjC / Ada / Fortran / COBOL / Haskell / OCaml ELF | plain ELF for header ids; base64 `SENGR` (offset = the `S`) or RAW (offset = the `H`); COBOL/Haskell config in PK19/RS20 overlay; OCaml HCFG in plugin `.data` |\n| File size > `e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize` | OVERLAY: `xxd -s <image_end> F`; magic `<2 caps><day>` or bare record; parse header fields the question lists, verify hash |\n| `\\0asm` | `lib.binary.wasm_layout` / `wasm-objdump -x`; `wasm`/`wasm32`; HCFG RAW in data segment 0 |\n| `kind: enum` + rule list, or text describing bytes | the question IS the spec (D17, D19, D30): implement it literally, emit one listed token |\n| **Single `flag` answer, \"crackme\", per-team build, 3 wrong max (D30 SHA1-Hulud)** | static strings/decoders first (answer-first), then EMULATE (Speakeasy / unicorn) with a PLAUSIBLE host, hook the final compare, differential probes; see Pitfalls |\n| Packed / `UPX!` / real code reversing | `lib.binary.packer_info` -> `upx -d` on a COPY; `rizin -q -c \"aaa; pdf @ sym.<fn>\"`; Ghidra headless (last resort) |\n\n## Day by day\n**D1-D16** (one language/day): D1 C ELF headers/`.huntress`/recover_code (~14 min, 4 wrong); D2 C++ ELF/MinGW PE, first HCFG,\nPE symbols = COMDAT `.text$<mangled>`; D3 .NET `pe_cli` after ~50 synonyms (~1 h 48 min); D4 Go `amd64` REJECTED -> `x86-64`;\nD6 jar constant-pool base64; D8 Swift 67 MB + backfill #1 + integer elf_class/machine; D9 Nim raw decoys + `hcfg_offset`; D10\n`has_hcfg_section`; D12 HCFG RAW; D14 ObjC `.hcfg`; D15 stripped/symbolized `<qualifier>_` ids; D16 wasm pair `wasm`/`wasm32`.\n**D17 \"Decoder Ring\"**: Ada + backfill #2; `hcfg_storage` burned ~10.9k POSTs / 3.5 h until the contract revision (enum).\n**D18-D23** (T+11 s .. T+2:25): Fortran; GnuCOBOL + `PK19` overlay (questions spelled the stub); Haskell + `RS20`\n(`hcfg_resource_size`); OCaml loader + `.cmxs` (question-named routing AFTER the tag peel); F# + support DLL (\"FIRST record that\nvalidates\"); VB.NET PE overlay (timed modes re-shaped values).\n**D24-D27** (T+35..80 s, 0 wrong): Scala/Clojure twin jars (12-id twin template; D25 Mastery `id(bytes)` cache cross-wiring);\nGroovy + `crash/trace.json` theme ASKED; V gcc/tcc twins, RAW HCFG at image_end, \"scan backward from the end\" (zero new code).\n**D28 \"Family Resemblance\"** (392 Qs; T+3:23, 6 rejected POSTs): Odin trio, family consensus \"do not use false-friend.elf\";\nBACKFILL #3 (54 spec-worded ids) sank 4 all-or-nothing batches on d20 `overlay_size` and d13 `crystal_symbol_count`.\n\n**D29 \"Fraternal Twins\"** (406 Qs; **CORRECT T+1:20, 0 rejected**; TT 3.0 s / Mastery 13 sets 5.7 s, first POST).\n- Artifact: FreeBASIC (fbc) ELF pair `d29--sample-O0.elf`, `-O3.elf` (43,931 B each, glibc dynamic, not stripped, `crtstuff.c` +\n  fbc rtlib FILE symbols; the two differ in only 12 bytes despite the O-level names). HCFG RAW appended at EOF-387.\n- 14 new ids: 2 sha256, `unoptimized_`/`optimized_` format + machine (integer 62), 4 consensus config_* (\"Decode both d29-- role\n  members and require ... byte-for-byte equal\"), 4 `optimized_config_*`. Insight: the id tags are WORDS, the basenames carry `O0`/\n  `O3`; the question's \"basename ends O3.elf\" routed them. Theme (optimization accounting / semantic equivalence) unasked; trace\n  family `freebasic_optimization_variant_trace`. Carried-over solver banked 392, then 6 + 8 new ids.\n\n**D30 \"Campaign Trail\"** (420 Qs; **CORRECT T+1:18**, 10 rejected = the race harness's `none` placeholder probes on the d30\nconfig ids, 0 real wrong answers; TT 3.1 s / Mastery 14 sets (5880 ids) 6.1 s, first POST).\n- Artifact: Haxe 4.3.7 -> Neko bytecode trio in archive order `d30--sample-config.n`, `-library.n`, `-loader.n` (20.9 KB each,\n  `NEKO` header identical, Haxe std paths `std/neko/*.hx` leak the organizer's build dir). Each ends with a RAW `HGRF` record\n  (ver 1, xor key e.g. 0xf1, ~695 B JSON, 0 bytes after it): `huntress.binary.campaign_graph.v1` {campaign_id `DAY30-000`, nodes\n  [loader.n, library.n, config.n], edges `loader.n->library.n`, `library.n->config.n`, load_order, config{...}, this_role\n  loader/library/config, network none, effects `isolated_multi_process_event_graph_only`}; no HCFG in any member.\n- 14 new ids: 3 sha256, `loader_`/`library_`/`config_capsule_` format (`neko_bytecode`, first try), 4 consensus config_* (\"Use\n  loader.n's decoded HGRF graph.config object after confirming all three canonical campaign graphs match when this_role is\n  omitted\"), 4 `config_capsule_graph_config_*` (config.n's own record).\n- Key insight: read the record path literally but resolve `graph.` as the record name (JSON top level has `config`, no `graph`);\n  normalise by deleting `this_role` before the 3-way equality. Tools: `xxd -l 16`, `grep -abo HGRF`, a 15-line rfind+crc+xor\n  decoder; ~40 lines added to the cumulative solver (`graph_record`, `d30_graph`). Graph edges/load order NOT asked.\n- **Bonus \"SHA1-Hulud\"** (flag crackme, see header): our 4 worker launches (~1 h 45 min, 0 wrong submits) did not get the flag;\n  a reviewer's manual analysis solved it in ~5 min (CORRECT T+2:20 from release). Lost time: an emulator with \"clean = not found\"\n  env stubs ran to completion SILENTLY on every input (env answers feed the keys -> poisoned target), read as \"gate bailed\";\n  25 min modelling SHA-1 stub variants that only needed to execute; byte-at-a-time attack defeated by the backwards second pass.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n| Field family | Accepted form | Rejected (never resubmit) |\n|---|---|---|\n| elf_class | exact_text: `ELF64`/`ELF32`; `kind: integer` (D8+): `64`/`32` | ELFCLASS64; `2`/`1` |\n| machine (`kind: integer`, role members D15-D30) | decimal e_machine (`62`), also ET_DYN `.cmxs`, every compiler/O-level | — |\n| endianness | `little` / `big` | little endian, lsb, msb |\n| machine (ELF exact_text) | `x86-64`, `x86`, `AArch64`, `ARM` (D19+ text: tool labels and codes also accepted) | EM_X86_64, x86_64, amd64 |\n| machine (PE FILE_HEADER) | 0x14c -> `i386`; 0x8664 -> `x86-64` | x86 (PE i386); raw `0x8664` |\n| architecture | the same machine words (Go amd64 -> `x86-64`) | amd64, arm64, 386, x86_64 |\n| elf_type | `ET_EXEC` / `ET_DYN` | EXEC |\n| entry_point, crc32_hex, xor_key_hex | lowercase hex with `0x` (crc `0x%08x`, key `0x%02x`) | — |\n| recover_code (`kind: integer`) | base-10 integer (`mov eax, 0x1fa4` -> 8100); `none` if the symbol is absent | the stripped leaf's constant |\n| has_* | enum `true`/`false` | — |\n| marker | exact `.huntress` string without the NUL; `none` if missing | — |\n| format (enum) | `elf`, `pe`, `pe_cli`, `jar`, `wasm`, **`neko_bytecode` (D30 Haxe->Neko `.n`, CONFIRMED)** | ELF, ELF64, exe, pe32+, jar_jvm, ~50 .NET synonyms |\n| format / arch per container | compiled ELF any language/compiler/O-level `elf`/`x86-64`; WASM `wasm`/`wasm32`; .NET any language `pe_cli`/`i386`; any JVM jar `jar`; Neko `neko_bytecode` | x86 for PE i386 |\n| C++ symbols ELF / PE | bare Itanium mangled name / COMDAT section name `.text$<mangled>` | demangled; bare on PE |\n| section_names (JSON) | pyelftools order INCLUDING the leading `\"\"` | list without \"\" (pre-D17) |\n| symbols / disassembly (JSON) | non-empty .symtab names, table order, dupes kept / capstone intel `\"mov eax, 8100\"`, `\"ret\"` | hex imm, `\"ret \"` |\n| methods / access_flags / method_count (jar) | Main-Class method_info names incl. `<init>` / decimal `49` / count incl. synthetics (d26 = 10) | — |\n| crash_fault_method / crash_frames_match_methods | trace.json `frames[0]` verbatim / set inclusion `true`/`false` | — |\n| metadata_version | BSJB root string `v4.0.30319` | net8.0 / TFM |\n| config_* (HCFG) | verbatim from decoded JSON (mutex ONE backslash); consensus of the NAMED members; D19 from the unpacked overlay | JSON-escaped `\\\\`; `none` when merely hidden |\n| config_* (HGRF, D30) | `graph.config.<key>` = decoded record JSON `[\"config\"][key]` verbatim; unqualified = loader.n after this_role-less 3-way match; `config_capsule_graph_config_*` = config.n's own record | `none` placeholders (10 rejected) |\n| hcfg_version / xor_key_hex / hcfg_offset | header byte 4 decimal / byte 5 `0x%02x` / decimal FILE offset (`S` base64, `H` raw) | — |\n| overlay_offset / overlay_size / hcfg_resource_size | last occurrence of the day's magic / len - that offset / RS20 u32le @+8 | non-day magic (19) |\n| hcfg_storage (enum, D17) | `base64`, `raw_hcfg_section`, `raw_const_array`, `wasm_data_segment`, `raw` | every free-text spelling (~10.9k probes) |\n| compression_methods (jar, json) | sorted distinct ZIP method ids `[0,8]` | — |\n| backfill #3 counts / hashes / header text (D28) | `.symtab` nonempty names (`.dynsym` only if none); `section_count` = e_shnum incl. 0 (PE: NumberOfSections); sorted LF-join sha256; colon-join of member digests; `cli_runtime` `2.5`; `packing_key_1/2_hex` `0x%02x` | d13 count with `.dynsym` (1255) |\n| flag (bonus crackme, D30) | the accepted INPUT itself, `flag{<32 hex>}` (program prints \"correct, the flag is \" + input) | decoys that also print correct (`your flag is in another castle`, short `flag{nic...`) -- never submitted |\nNaming law: native format = container only; managed .NET = `pe_cli`; Java broke it (`jar`); VM bytecode = `<vm>_bytecode`.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **A synthetic label with no derivable spelling** (D3 ~1.5 h; D17 `hcfg_storage` ~10.9k POSTs): stop after ~10 single-id probes\n  plus one `hctf labels` run, write HELP.md, RE-PULL THE CONTRACT periodically and diff each id. Never mass-probe exact_text.\n- **Reversing what the question already specifies** (D19): read the longest question of each new family FIRST; size fields =\n  the exact header field the layout names. D30: the HGRF layout, scan direction and normalisation were all in the question.\n- **Absence vs hidden**: `none`/`[]`/`false` only when ABSENT (stripped d01), wrong when merely HIDDEN (D19 packed config; D30\n  race-harness `none` placeholders for the HGRF config ids -> 10 rejected probes, harmless but useless: a new record magic means\n  \"decode it\", not \"absent\").\n- **A multi-field POST is all-or-nothing** (D2, D28): POST carried-over ids first (they bank), then each NEW field family alone\n  or bisect on the first rejection; a heuristic answer to a new spec is a guess until accepted.\n- **Routing**: peel the longest multi-word member tag, but when the tag is a semantic word (`optimized`, `config_capsule`) map it\n  through the question's \"basename ends X\"; mind substring tags (`unoptimized` ⊃ `optimized`); a field that starts with `config`\n  after a role tag (`config_capsule_graph_config_url`) is still a role field. Read `answer_format.kind` per id.\n- **JSON paths in questions** (D30 `graph.config.campaign`): the first segment may name the RECORD, not a key -- resolve against\n  the decoded object, dropping a non-key leading segment; never answer `none` because `obj[\"graph\"]` is missing.\n- **\"The theme is never asked\" is NOT a rule** (D26): list every member's NON-code entries (`unzip -l`, sections, resources,\n  overlays, tail records) and parse any JSON sidecar up front. Unasked D27-D30 beyond routing; record theme facts in NOTES.md.\n- **Per-member caches keyed on `id(bytes)`** (D25 Mastery, 55 wrong ids): key on (delivery, member name) / sha256. Symptom: a\n  rejected value that is VALID for another group of the same delivery.\n- **Archives**: never unzip recursively; jar members are deflated (`grep HCFG file.jar` finds nothing) -- inflate every entry.\n  Huge members (D8 67 MB): cheap encodings first, crc-gate every hit.\n- **Decoy magics** (D9): code that checks the magic embeds `\"HCFG\"` literals; len 0 => crc32(b\"\")==0 passes. Require non-empty\n  JSON; scan DIRECTION per question (D22 first-from-start, D27-D30 backward from EOF); offsets from `re.finditer().start()`.\n- **ELF-worded id on a PE re-roll** (D28 TT d10): every ELF header/section/symbol field needs a PE mapping.\n- **Crackme with no oracle (D30 SHA1-Hulud)**: (1) SILENCE on every input under emulation = environment answers feed the keys,\n  not \"my input is wrong\": make every fingerprint report a PLAUSIBLE real host (4+ CPUs, 8 GB, 1920x1080, no hypervisor bit\n  CPUID 0x40000000, no tool processes/drivers/registry markers, coherent RDTSC/QPC/KUSER clocks, sane LastError) -- a \"not found\"\n  stub is a value; (2) MEASURE before reversing: run two different probes, diff every operand stream at the final compare\n  (inputs-invariant streams = stored target/masks), then ask which keys depend on input; (3) chained-block ciphers (key_j from\n  plaintext block j-1): decode block 0 from any probe, extend the probe progressively (8 -> 24 -> 38 chars; probe length must\n  equal the target's length word); (4) OR-verdicts carry decoys: enumerate every accepted group, submit only the `flag{32hex}`\n  one; (5) self-hashing `.text`: never byte-patch, hook in the emulator or shadow `.text`; (6) don't re-implement a hash you\n  only need to execute; skip deliberate slow loops instead. Speakeasy (Windows PE emulator with API/PEB/TEB stubs) saves the\n  scaffolding; never run the sample natively.\n- **Timed windows**: download dominates (D16 TT 52 s of 64 s). WASM sizes = 5-byte PADDED LEB128; PE machine map must include\n  0x8664 -> `x86-64`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":419,"cache_read_input_tokens":120446,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":419},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"231816e3-d655-4fc4-9734-2a09a078ac00","uuid":"ebe7bc84-4baa-4483-a0b0-8160b0b5d5be","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:42:43.425Z","request_id":"req_011CgZczCvjXZTQpgBSJojWp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0162NLqqYNewcDT11DeSdpNN":{"file_path":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md","content":"# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-30; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (OBSERVATIONS, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, D8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations\"): solvers derive structure, degrade per field.\n- One `evidence.zip` (AES, password `infected`), CUMULATIVE from D3: one group per past day (`dNN--sample.<ext>`, `variant-000`\n  before D22) + ONE new container/language per day: D1 C ELF, D2 C++ (ELF/MinGW PE32+), D3 .NET, D4 Go, D5 Rust, D6 Java jar,\n  D7 Kotlin jar, D8 Swift (67 MB), D9 Nim, D10 Zig, D11 D, D12 FPC, D13 Crystal, D14 ObjC, D15 C `-stripped`/`-symbolized`, D16\n  WASM `-compact`/`-direct`, D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL + `PK19` overlay, D20 Haskell + `RS20` overlay, D21 OCaml\n  `-loader.elf` + `-plugin.cmxs`, D22 F# (+ `FSharp.Core.dll`), D23 VB.NET, D24 Scala jar PAIR `-vulnerable`/`-corrected`, D25\n  Clojure jar PAIR, D26 Groovy jar (+ `crash/trace.json`), D27 V ELF PAIR `-gcc.elf`/`-tcc.elf`, D28 Odin ELF TRIO `-family-a`/\n  `-family-b`/`-false-friend`, **D29 FreeBASIC ELF PAIR `-O0.elf`/`-O3.elf` (43.9 KB each, glibc, not stripped, differ in 12\n  bytes), D30 Haxe->Neko bytecode TRIO `-loader.n`/`-library.n`/`-config.n` (~20.9 KB each, magic `NEKO`; first VM-bytecode\n  member since WASM; the D19 enum token `neko_bytecode` finally shipped)**.\n  Since D18 each day = a THEME on a new language: call graph, packing, overlays, shared libs, managed<->native bridge, anti-\n  analysis, PATCH DIFF (D24), BOUNDS ROOT CAUSE (D25), CRASH TRIAGE (D26), COMPILER ATTRIBUTION (D27), FAMILY CLUSTERING (D28),\n  **OPTIMIZATION EQUIVALENCE (D29 \"Two binaries, same source, different compiler moods ... prove they're semantically the same\n  program\"), CAMPAIGN GRAPH (D30 \"Reconstruct the loader, library, and config graph across the whole set and map the operation\n  end to end\")**. D31 is the LAST day: expect a capstone \"across the whole set\" (D30's wording already says it) and/or backfill #4.\n- Ids `dNN_artifact_sha256_K` / `dNN_analysis_<field>`; multi-member groups add `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>`. **The `<tag>` is NOT\n  always the basename token**: D21-D28 tag = basename role (`family-a` -> `family_a`), but D29 `unoptimized_`/`optimized_` route to\n  `-O0.elf`/`-O3.elf` and D30 `config_capsule_` routes to `-config.n` -- the QUESTION says \"Use the unique dNN-- member whose\n  basename ends O3.elf\": route on that sentence first, tag second. Unqualified ids = consensus of the members the question names.\n- From D2 every new member embeds the **HCFG** blob `'HCFG' | u8 ver | u8 xor_key | u16le len | u32le crc32(plain) | xor'd JSON\n  @12`; only its STORAGE changes (Variant axes). **D30 changed the MAGIC: `HGRF` (same 12-byte layout) carrying a campaign-graph\n  JSON with the config NESTED under `config`** -- scan for any `[A-Z]{4}` + this header that crc-validates, not only `HCFG`.\n- The hard part is the GM's label for `exact_text` fields; **the organizers RE-ISSUE the contract** when a label is unguessable\n  (D17 `hcfg_storage` -> enum). Since D24 EVERY question is a full SPEC (layout, scan direction, member choice, JSON path).\n- **The contract LEAKS future days**: D19 \"RS20 for Day 20\", d07 \"for Day 26 use the primary classfile\", enum `neko_bytecode`\n  (D19 -> shipped D30). All came true. After D30 no unseen token/day number remains -- re-grep the D31 contract anyway.\n- **Theme asked on its own group only sometimes**: D19/D20 yes, D21-D25 no, D26 yes (JSON sidecar), D27 no, D28/D29/D30 ONLY via\n  routing + consensus (no similarity, optimization or graph-edge id; D30 asked graph.config.* but not nodes/edges/load_order).\n  14 ids per group since D28 (sha256 per member + `<role>_format`/`<role>_machine` + 4 consensus config_* + role config_*).\n- **Every member embeds a `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` template** (unasked) whose `family` names the theme: D25\n  `clojure_bounds_root_cause_trace`, D26 `groovy_synthetic_crash_trace`, D27 `v_cross_backend_attribution_trace`, D28\n  `odin_family_cluster_trace`, D29 `freebasic_optimization_variant_trace`/`semantic_equivalence_only`; D30 puts the theme in the\n  HGRF record itself (`schema huntress.binary.campaign_graph.v1`, `effects isolated_multi_process_event_graph_only`).\n- Question count: 80 on D8, +10/day to 160, D17 204, +12/day to D27 324, D28 392 = 28 x 14 (backfill #3), **D29 406, D30 420\n  (+14/day, no new backfill)**. Mastery = `setN.` copies, +1 set/day (D28 12, D29 13 = 5278 ids, D30 14 = 5880 ids). Timed:\n  D28 TT 54 s; **D29 TT 3.0 s / M 5.7 s; D30 TT 3.1 s / M 6.1 s (all CORRECT first POST)**.\n- **Bonus flag challenge (D30 \"SHA1-Hulud\", separate slug)**: ONE `flag` answer, per-team build, 3 wrong submissions max, a\n  hardened Rust PE64 crackme (self-hashing `.text`, anti-debug, env fingerprint FED INTO THE KEYS, CBC-style two-pass cipher,\n  OR-verdict with decoys). Organizers: Day-30 only. Method is in Pitfalls (`reference/D30_SHA1HULUD_LESSONS.md` = full write-up).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, storage per container: `.hcfg` section (D2/D10/D14), .NET FieldRVA (D3), Go/Rust\n  rodata, base64 in a jar constant pool (Java/Kotlin; Scala `$` module, Clojure `<ns>__init` `encoded-config`, Groovy\n  `encodedConfig`) / Swift/Nim/D/Crystal literal, RAW FPC `.data`, WASM data seg 0, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`, D19 packed overlay,\n  D20 RS20 overlay, D21 plugin `.data`, D22 RAW twice (`.text` + PE overlay), D23 PE overlay, D27-D29 RAW appended at\n  `e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize` (file ends with the record; \"Scan backward from the end ... first CRC32-valid\"), **D30 HGRF RAW at\n  the END of each Neko `.n` (tail 0 bytes, no ELF section table to compute image_end)**. Rule: scan for `HCFG`/`SENGR...` (jars:\n  every class's constant pool) AND any record magic the question names, accept only crc32(plain) match AND parsing JSON, keep\n  scanning past failures (D9 decoys); scan in the DIRECTION the question states. Storage never changed WITHIN a day.\n- **Record magic / payload schema (D30)** -- `HGRF` = `HCFG` layout (\"byte-4 version, byte-5 XOR key, little-endian length and\n  CRC32 ... same 12-byte layout as HCFG\"); JSON = `{schema, campaign_id, nodes[], edges[\"a->b\"], load_order[], config{campaign,\n  domain, ipv4, url, mutex, windows_path, linux_path, service, host_model}, this_role, network, effects}`. The question's path\n  `graph.config.campaign` names the RECORD first: `graph` is NOT a JSON key -> drop a leading segment that is not a key and names\n  the record (graph/record/root/<magic>), then walk the dots. Consensus: \"confirm all three canonical campaign graphs match when\n  this_role is omitted\" = drop `this_role`, compare canonical JSON of all members, answer from the member named (loader.n).\n- **Overlay layout per day (D19 PK19, D20 RS20)** -- appended at image end, magic `<2 caps><day>`, header spelled by the QUESTION:\n  PK19 `magic|ver|k1|k2|pad|u32le packed_len @8|sha256 @12|packed @44`, unpack `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`; RS20 `magic|ver|u32le\n  resource_len @8|u16le scratch_len @12|sha256(scratch) @16|HCFG @48|scratch`. Rule: `rfind(magic)`, parse listed widths, verify.\n- **Location / storage as answer** -- `hcfg_offset` = decimal FILE offset (base64 -> the `S`, RAW -> the `H`); `overlay_offset`\n  = the magic, `overlay_size` = len - offset; `hcfg_resource_size` = u32le @+8. `hcfg_storage` enum in order: `base64` ->\n  `raw_hcfg_section` -> `wasm_data_segment` -> `raw_const_array` -> `raw`.\n- **Any other encoding -> `lib.binary.hcfg_scan(data)`** (hex/b32/b85/UTF-16/reversed/xor/zlib/rolling xor/custom b64/split/\n  int-array/strided/RC4/AES/TEA/ChaCha/stack-built); `hcfg_find` = first valid hit.\n- **Config VALUE SHAPES** -- crc, key and values re-roll per variant; timed modes change the SHAPE: campaign `BRNN-000` ->\n  `BRNN-<8 HEX>` (D28 false friend `FF28-`), domain `variant-000.dayNN...` (D29) / `campaign-000.day30...` (D30) ->\n  `<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid`, mutex `Global\\HuntressBRNN-000[_000]` -> `Global\\Huntress<12 HEX>`, url `.../v/BR29-000`\n  / `.../stage/BR30-000` -> `https://<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid/<word>/<10hex>`; one word pool (sync/hub/core/mesh/relay/\n  stage/edge/cache/vault/proxy/node/gate) drawn independently for domain, url host, url path. Extra keys appear without warning\n  (D28 `host_model`/`ipv4`; D30 `windows_path`/`linux_path`/`service`). Rule: copy verbatim; never regex-check a shape.\n- **Container per member** -- ELF vs PE32+ re-rolls per member in Mastery (d02, d04, d10); dispatch on MAGIC (`7f454c46`, `MZ`,\n  `PK`, `\\0asm`, `NEKO`). The format question spells the rule (\"Classify final bytes by magic and parsed container ... neko_bytecode\n  for NEKO bytecode\"). ELF-worded ids still apply to a PE re-roll (D28 TT d10: `section_count` = NumberOfSections).\n- **Member routing** -- (1) id tag = longest `[^a-z0-9]+` token naming exactly one member (multi-word: `family_a`, `false_friend`,\n  `config_capsule`); (2) the question's \"basename ends X\" / \"Use the dNN-- X member\" wins when the tag is a SEMANTIC word that is\n  not in any basename (D29 `optimized` -> `O3.elf`, `unoptimized` -> `O0.elf`, substring trap: `unoptimized` contains `optimized`;\n  D30 `config_capsule` -> `config.n`); (3) the tag can precede the field family (`corrected_config_url`) and the field can itself\n  start with `config` (`config_capsule_graph_config_campaign` = member `config.n`, field `graph.config.campaign`). `sha256_K` =\n  ARCHIVE order, never sorted. Question-named routing runs AFTER the tag peel (D21 dropped 26 ids otherwise).\n- **Unqualified id over a named subset (D24-D30)** -- \"Decode both dNN-- role members and require their config objects to be\n  byte-for-byte equal\" (D24/D25/D27/D29), D28 \"Decode family-a.elf and family-b.elf ... do not use false-friend.elf\", D30 \"Use\n  loader.n's decoded HGRF graph.config object after confirming all three ... match when this_role is omitted\": decode exactly the\n  named members, normalise as told, assert equal, answer from the named one. The excluded look-alike has its OWN valid config.\n- **Theme sidecar inside the member (D26)** -- jar entry `crash/trace.json` (`huntress.synthetic_crash.v1`, frames innermost-\n  first); entry whose name ends `trace.json`, answer frames[0]; \"every frame in the primary classfile method-name set\" = inclusion.\n- **Primary vs support members (D3, D22, D23)** -- primary assembly = the `.dll` that is not a framework/dependency (FSharp.Core,\n  System.*, Microsoft.*); hash ALL members. Basenames: `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*` since D22.\n- **Stripped carry-over d01** -- re-rolls stripped in some sets: symbols/disassembly `[]`, has_symtab `false`, recover_code `none`.\n- **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` ids (D30 14 sets), each its own delivery; each set's 1st question ends `Evidence case:\n  dNN-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]` = set->delivery map. Per-member caches key on (delivery, member name)\n  or sha256, never `id(bytes)` (D25: 5/9 sets cross-wired).\n- **kind / field sets per group** -- `elf_class`/`machine` exact_text on d01 but INTEGER on d08/d15/d21+ (dispatch on\n  `answer_format.kind`); old groups gain ids over days (D8, D17, D28): answer by field name from THAT member's facts dict.\n- **Backfill #3 spec grammar (D28, 54 ids on d01-d27)** -- public substring predicates (Latin-1 [+UTF-16LE]), regex counts over\n  NONEMPTY `.symtab` names (`.dynsym` only when no `.symtab`: d13 771 not 1255), sorted LF-join sha256 (UNIQUE names for\n  `method_names_sha256`), colon-join of member digests, Jcc byte scans in `.text`, `cli_runtime` Major.Minor, `section_count`,\n  PK19 keys, size ids w/o a named magic = the day's own overlay magic (d20 `overlay_size` = len - rfind(`RS20`)). Rule:\n  implement the sentence literally (`lib.binary.generic_field`). No backfill #4 on D29/D30.\n- **Speed flags (no answer change)** -- CPU contention: re-measure with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py`;\n  floor = inflate + sha256 of every member (all asked); D30 single solve phase 1.3 s, 14-set Mastery 1.5 s.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"AES Encrypted\" | `7z x -pinfected -y evidence.zip` (Python: `pyzipper`); `sha256sum *` for every `artifact_sha256_K` (archive order within the group) |\n| `readelf -h -S` hint, ELF header questions | `readelf -hSW`, `readelf -sW`; `readelf -p .huntress` for the custom-section `marker` (D1, re-asked D17) |\n| \"constant returned by recover_code\" / `disassembly` | `objdump -d -M intel --no-show-raw-insn` around `<recover_code>`; capstone on the FUNC symbol's bytes |\n| Stripped C build, no `.symtab` | answer the absence the question defines (`[]`/`none`); recon only: leaf `b8 imm32 c3` (`lib.binary.recover_return_constants`) |\n| C++ / \"mangled\" / \"vtable\" / \"RTTI\" | `nm -C` / `c++filt`; `_ZTV`/`_ZTI`/`_ZTS`; PE: `objdump -t file.exe` (COMDAT `.text$<mangled>`) |\n| `PE32+` MinGW `.exe` | `objdump -t` (COFF symbols), `pefile` (Machine, OPTIONAL_HEADER.Magic, sections incl. `.hcfg`) |\n| .NET (`BSJB`, `.runtimeconfig.json`; F# `FSharp.Core`, VB.NET `Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core`) | `ilspycmd` / `dnfile`; `pe_cli`/`i386`/`v4.0.30319`; PRIMARY dll only; raw `grep -abo HCFG` -> first crc-valid hit |\n| P/Invoke / \"bridge\" (`DllImportAttribute`, ModuleRef) | dnfile `md.ModuleRef`, `md.ImplMap` rows; `ilspycmd` for `[DllImport]` signatures |\n| Anti-analysis predicates (Debugger/Stopwatch/Environment TypeRefs, env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`) | NEVER run it: asked ids are header + HCFG (static); record the predicate list |\n| Go / Rust | `go version -m f`, `lib.binary.go_buildinfo`/`go_pclntab_funcs`; Rust: header + `HCFG` scan, `rustfilt` |\n| `.jar` (Java/Kotlin/Scala/Clojure/Groovy, `Created-By: Huntress deterministic <Lang> factory`) | unzip, Main-Class, `javap -v -p`; HCFG base64 `ldc` may be in Scala `Foo$`, Clojure `<ns>__init`, Groovy `encodedConfig`; `unzip -l` for NON-class sidecars |\n| Crash artifact (`crash/trace.json`, `core`, `*.dmp`, hs_err, ASan) | `jq . trace.json` (frames innermost-first); native: `readelf -n core` -> RIP -> `addr2line -f -e bin`; capstone the faulting insn |\n| Twin/role members (`-stripped`/`-symbolized`, `-loader`/`-plugin`, `-vulnerable`/`-corrected`, `-gcc`/`-tcc`, `-O0`/`-O3`) | route `<tag>_` ids (tag may be a semantic word: `optimized` = `-O3`); diff if asked: `javap -p -c` / `objdump -d` per symbol + `diff`, `rz-diff -t functions a b` |\n| N look-alikes (`-family-a`/`-family-b`/`-false-friend`) | `cmp -l A B \\| wc -l` per pair (D28 twins 1 byte, stranger ~2k), per-member HCFG (stranger `FF28-`); consensus = NAMED members only |\n| V / Odin / FreeBASIC ELF (`main__main`+`builtin__*`; `/odin/base/runtime/*.odin`; fbc rtlib `dev_scrn_init.c`/`dev_scrn_write.c` FILE syms, `fb_*`) | plain ELF (`elf`/62); HCFG RAW at image_end (`grep -abo HCFG F`), \"scan backward from the end\" |\n| **`NEKO` magic / `.n` members (D30: Haxe 4.3.7 build, strings `std/neko/*.hx`, globals `@classes`/`@Loader`/`@String`; header `NEKO` + u32le nglobals/nfields/codesize)** | format `neko_bytecode`; config record RAW at EOF: `grep -abo 'HGRF\\|HCFG' F`, rfind + crc gate; JSON path from the question (`graph.config.X` -> obj[\"config\"][\"X\"]); `nekoc`/`haxe` only for theme facts |\n| Record magic you have not seen (`HGRF`, next ???) \"uses the same 12-byte layout as HCFG\" | generic 4-byte-magic record decoder: magic\\|ver\\|key\\|u16 len\\|u32 crc\\|xor payload; scan direction + member from the question |\n| Backfill \"Evaluate this public predicate\", \"count names that match /re/\", \"sort ... SHA-256\" | `lib.binary.generic_field(blob, suffix, question, member)`; `.symtab` only (`.dynsym` if none) |\n| Same-source builds named by COMPILER or FLAGS, \"name the toolchain\", \"account for every optimization\" | header + consensus HCFG (asked D27/D29). Facts if asked: `readelf --debug-dump=info F \\| grep -m2 producer`, `.comment`, gcc IPA suffixes, tcc `.stab`, PT_INTERP libc; O-level: function count/inlining, `.text` size |\n| Swift ELF (`swift5_*`, 60+ MB) | never eager-parse symbols; regex `SENGR` base64 in `.rodata`; `bin/swift-demangle` |\n| Nim / D / Crystal / FPC / ObjC / Ada / Fortran / COBOL / Haskell / OCaml ELF | plain ELF for header ids; base64 `SENGR` (offset = the `S`) or RAW (offset = the `H`); COBOL/Haskell config in PK19/RS20 overlay; OCaml HCFG in plugin `.data` |\n| File size > `e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize` | OVERLAY: `xxd -s <image_end> F`; magic `<2 caps><day>` or bare record; parse header fields the question lists, verify hash |\n| `\\0asm` | `lib.binary.wasm_layout` / `wasm-objdump -x`; `wasm`/`wasm32`; HCFG RAW in data segment 0 |\n| `kind: enum` + rule list, or text describing bytes | the question IS the spec (D17, D19, D30): implement it literally, emit one listed token |\n| **Single `flag` answer, \"crackme\", per-team build, 3 wrong max (D30 SHA1-Hulud)** | static strings/decoders first (answer-first), then EMULATE (Speakeasy / unicorn) with a PLAUSIBLE host, hook the final compare, differential probes; see Pitfalls |\n| Packed / `UPX!` / real code reversing | `lib.binary.packer_info` -> `upx -d` on a COPY; `rizin -q -c \"aaa; pdf @ sym.<fn>\"`; Ghidra headless (last resort) |\n\n## Day by day\n**D1-D16** (one language/day): D1 C ELF headers/`.huntress`/recover_code (~14 min, 4 wrong); D2 C++ ELF/MinGW PE, first HCFG,\nPE symbols = COMDAT `.text$<mangled>`; D3 .NET `pe_cli` after ~50 synonyms (~1 h 48 min); D4 Go `amd64` REJECTED -> `x86-64`;\nD6 jar constant-pool base64; D8 Swift 67 MB + backfill #1 + integer elf_class/machine; D9 Nim raw decoys + `hcfg_offset`; D10\n`has_hcfg_section`; D12 HCFG RAW; D14 ObjC `.hcfg`; D15 stripped/symbolized `<qualifier>_` ids; D16 wasm pair `wasm`/`wasm32`.\n**D17 \"Decoder Ring\"**: Ada + backfill #2; `hcfg_storage` burned ~10.9k POSTs / 3.5 h until the contract revision (enum).\n**D18-D23** (T+11 s .. T+2:25): Fortran; GnuCOBOL + `PK19` overlay (questions spelled the stub); Haskell + `RS20`\n(`hcfg_resource_size`); OCaml loader + `.cmxs` (question-named routing AFTER the tag peel); F# + support DLL (\"FIRST record that\nvalidates\"); VB.NET PE overlay (timed modes re-shaped values).\n**D24-D27** (T+35..80 s, 0 wrong): Scala/Clojure twin jars (12-id twin template; D25 Mastery `id(bytes)` cache cross-wiring);\nGroovy + `crash/trace.json` theme ASKED; V gcc/tcc twins, RAW HCFG at image_end, \"scan backward from the end\" (zero new code).\n**D28 \"Family Resemblance\"** (392 Qs; T+3:23, 6 rejected POSTs): Odin trio, family consensus \"do not use false-friend.elf\";\nBACKFILL #3 (54 spec-worded ids) sank 4 all-or-nothing batches on d20 `overlay_size` and d13 `crystal_symbol_count`.\n\n**D29 \"Fraternal Twins\"** (406 Qs; **CORRECT T+1:20, 0 rejected**; TT 3.0 s / Mastery 13 sets 5.7 s, first POST).\n- Artifact: FreeBASIC (fbc) ELF pair `d29--sample-O0.elf`, `-O3.elf` (43,931 B each, glibc dynamic, not stripped, `crtstuff.c` +\n  fbc rtlib FILE symbols; the two differ in only 12 bytes despite the O-level names). HCFG RAW appended at EOF-387.\n- 14 new ids: 2 sha256, `unoptimized_`/`optimized_` format + machine (integer 62), 4 consensus config_* (\"Decode both d29-- role\n  members and require ... byte-for-byte equal\"), 4 `optimized_config_*`. Insight: the id tags are WORDS, the basenames carry `O0`/\n  `O3`; the question's \"basename ends O3.elf\" routed them. Theme (optimization accounting / semantic equivalence) unasked; trace\n  family `freebasic_optimization_variant_trace`. Carried-over solver banked 392, then 6 + 8 new ids.\n\n**D30 \"Campaign Trail\"** (420 Qs; **CORRECT T+1:18**, 10 rejected = the race harness's `none` placeholder probes on the d30\nconfig ids, 0 real wrong answers; TT 3.1 s / Mastery 14 sets (5880 ids) 6.1 s, first POST).\n- Artifact: Haxe 4.3.7 -> Neko bytecode trio in archive order `d30--sample-config.n`, `-library.n`, `-loader.n` (20.9 KB each,\n  `NEKO` header identical, Haxe std paths `std/neko/*.hx` leak the organizer's build dir). Each ends with a RAW `HGRF` record\n  (ver 1, xor key e.g. 0xf1, ~695 B JSON, 0 bytes after it): `huntress.binary.campaign_graph.v1` {campaign_id `DAY30-000`, nodes\n  [loader.n, library.n, config.n], edges `loader.n->library.n`, `library.n->config.n`, load_order, config{...}, this_role\n  loader/library/config, network none, effects `isolated_multi_process_event_graph_only`}; no HCFG in any member.\n- 14 new ids: 3 sha256, `loader_`/`library_`/`config_capsule_` format (`neko_bytecode`, first try), 4 consensus config_* (\"Use\n  loader.n's decoded HGRF graph.config object after confirming all three canonical campaign graphs match when this_role is\n  omitted\"), 4 `config_capsule_graph_config_*` (config.n's own record).\n- Key insight: read the record path literally but resolve `graph.` as the record name (JSON top level has `config`, no `graph`);\n  normalise by deleting `this_role` before the 3-way equality. Tools: `xxd -l 16`, `grep -abo HGRF`, a 15-line rfind+crc+xor\n  decoder; ~40 lines added to the cumulative solver (`graph_record`, `d30_graph`). Graph edges/load order NOT asked.\n- **Bonus \"SHA1-Hulud\"** (flag crackme, see header): our 4 worker launches (~1 h 45 min, 0 wrong submits) did not get the flag;\n  a reviewer's manual analysis solved it in ~5 min (CORRECT T+2:20 from release). Lost time: an emulator with \"clean = not found\"\n  env stubs ran to completion SILENTLY on every input (env answers feed the keys -> poisoned target), read as \"gate bailed\";\n  25 min modelling SHA-1 stub variants that only needed to execute; byte-at-a-time attack defeated by the backwards second pass.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n| Field family | Accepted form | Rejected (never resubmit) |\n|---|---|---|\n| elf_class | exact_text: `ELF64`/`ELF32`; `kind: integer` (D8+): `64`/`32` | ELFCLASS64; `2`/`1` |\n| machine (`kind: integer`, role members D15-D30) | decimal e_machine (`62`), also ET_DYN `.cmxs`, every compiler/O-level | — |\n| endianness | `little` / `big` | little endian, lsb, msb |\n| machine (ELF exact_text) | `x86-64`, `x86`, `AArch64`, `ARM` (D19+ text: tool labels and codes also accepted) | EM_X86_64, x86_64, amd64 |\n| machine (PE FILE_HEADER) | 0x14c -> `i386`; 0x8664 -> `x86-64` | x86 (PE i386); raw `0x8664` |\n| architecture | the same machine words (Go amd64 -> `x86-64`) | amd64, arm64, 386, x86_64 |\n| elf_type | `ET_EXEC` / `ET_DYN` | EXEC |\n| entry_point, crc32_hex, xor_key_hex | lowercase hex with `0x` (crc `0x%08x`, key `0x%02x`) | — |\n| recover_code (`kind: integer`) | base-10 integer (`mov eax, 0x1fa4` -> 8100); `none` if the symbol is absent | the stripped leaf's constant |\n| has_* | enum `true`/`false` | — |\n| marker | exact `.huntress` string without the NUL; `none` if missing | — |\n| format (enum) | `elf`, `pe`, `pe_cli`, `jar`, `wasm`, **`neko_bytecode` (D30 Haxe->Neko `.n`, CONFIRMED)** | ELF, ELF64, exe, pe32+, jar_jvm, ~50 .NET synonyms |\n| format / arch per container | compiled ELF any language/compiler/O-level `elf`/`x86-64`; WASM `wasm`/`wasm32`; .NET any language `pe_cli`/`i386`; any JVM jar `jar`; Neko `neko_bytecode` | x86 for PE i386 |\n| C++ symbols ELF / PE | bare Itanium mangled name / COMDAT section name `.text$<mangled>` | demangled; bare on PE |\n| section_names (JSON) | pyelftools order INCLUDING the leading `\"\"` | list without \"\" (pre-D17) |\n| symbols / disassembly (JSON) | non-empty .symtab names, table order, dupes kept / capstone intel `\"mov eax, 8100\"`, `\"ret\"` | hex imm, `\"ret \"` |\n| methods / access_flags / method_count (jar) | Main-Class method_info names incl. `<init>` / decimal `49` / count incl. synthetics (d26 = 10) | — |\n| crash_fault_method / crash_frames_match_methods | trace.json `frames[0]` verbatim / set inclusion `true`/`false` | — |\n| metadata_version | BSJB root string `v4.0.30319` | net8.0 / TFM |\n| config_* (HCFG) | verbatim from decoded JSON (mutex ONE backslash); consensus of the NAMED members; D19 from the unpacked overlay | JSON-escaped `\\\\`; `none` when merely hidden |\n| config_* (HGRF, D30) | `graph.config.<key>` = decoded record JSON `[\"config\"][key]` verbatim; unqualified = loader.n after this_role-less 3-way match; `config_capsule_graph_config_*` = config.n's own record | `none` placeholders (10 rejected) |\n| hcfg_version / xor_key_hex / hcfg_offset | header byte 4 decimal / byte 5 `0x%02x` / decimal FILE offset (`S` base64, `H` raw) | — |\n| overlay_offset / overlay_size / hcfg_resource_size | last occurrence of the day's magic / len - that offset / RS20 u32le @+8 | non-day magic (19) |\n| hcfg_storage (enum, D17) | `base64`, `raw_hcfg_section`, `raw_const_array`, `wasm_data_segment`, `raw` | every free-text spelling (~10.9k probes) |\n| compression_methods (jar, json) | sorted distinct ZIP method ids `[0,8]` | — |\n| backfill #3 counts / hashes / header text (D28) | `.symtab` nonempty names (`.dynsym` only if none); `section_count` = e_shnum incl. 0 (PE: NumberOfSections); sorted LF-join sha256; colon-join of member digests; `cli_runtime` `2.5`; `packing_key_1/2_hex` `0x%02x` | d13 count with `.dynsym` (1255) |\n| flag (bonus crackme, D30) | the accepted INPUT itself, `flag{<32 hex>}` (program prints \"correct, the flag is \" + input) | decoys that also print correct (`your flag is in another castle`, short `flag{nic...`) -- never submitted |\nNaming law: native format = container only; managed .NET = `pe_cli`; Java broke it (`jar`); VM bytecode = `<vm>_bytecode`.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **A synthetic label with no derivable spelling** (D3 ~1.5 h; D17 `hcfg_storage` ~10.9k POSTs): stop after ~10 single-id probes\n  plus one `hctf labels` run, write HELP.md, RE-PULL THE CONTRACT periodically and diff each id. Never mass-probe exact_text.\n- **Reversing what the question already specifies** (D19): read the longest question of each new family FIRST; size fields =\n  the exact header field the layout names. D30: the HGRF layout, scan direction and normalisation were all in the question.\n- **Absence vs hidden**: `none`/`[]`/`false` only when ABSENT (stripped d01), wrong when merely HIDDEN (D19 packed config; D30\n  race-harness `none` placeholders for the HGRF config ids -> 10 rejected probes, harmless but useless: a new record magic means\n  \"decode it\", not \"absent\").\n- **A multi-field POST is all-or-nothing** (D2, D28): POST carried-over ids first (they bank), then each NEW field family alone\n  or bisect on the first rejection; a heuristic answer to a new spec is a guess until accepted.\n- **Routing**: peel the longest multi-word member tag, but when the tag is a semantic word (`optimized`, `config_capsule`) map it\n  through the question's \"basename ends X\"; mind substring tags (`unoptimized` ⊃ `optimized`); a field that starts with `config`\n  after a role tag (`config_capsule_graph_config_url`) is still a role field. Read `answer_format.kind` per id.\n- **JSON paths in questions** (D30 `graph.config.campaign`): the first segment may name the RECORD, not a key -- resolve against\n  the decoded object, dropping a non-key leading segment; never answer `none` because `obj[\"graph\"]` is missing.\n- **\"The theme is never asked\" is NOT a rule** (D26): list every member's NON-code entries (`unzip -l`, sections, resources,\n  overlays, tail records) and parse any JSON sidecar up front. Unasked D27-D30 beyond routing; record theme facts in NOTES.md.\n- **Per-member caches keyed on `id(bytes)`** (D25 Mastery, 55 wrong ids): key on (delivery, member name) / sha256. Symptom: a\n  rejected value that is VALID for another group of the same delivery.\n- **Archives**: never unzip recursively; jar members are deflated (`grep HCFG file.jar` finds nothing) -- inflate every entry.\n  Huge members (D8 67 MB): cheap encodings first, crc-gate every hit.\n- **Decoy magics** (D9): code that checks the magic embeds `\"HCFG\"` literals; len 0 => crc32(b\"\")==0 passes. Require non-empty\n  JSON; scan DIRECTION per question (D22 first-from-start, D27-D30 backward from EOF); offsets from `re.finditer().start()`.\n- **ELF-worded id on a PE re-roll** (D28 TT d10): every ELF header/section/symbol field needs a PE mapping.\n- **Crackme with no oracle (D30 SHA1-Hulud)**: (1) SILENCE on every input under emulation = environment answers feed the keys,\n  not \"my input is wrong\": make every fingerprint report a PLAUSIBLE real host (4+ CPUs, 8 GB, 1920x1080, no hypervisor bit\n  CPUID 0x40000000, no tool processes/drivers/registry markers, coherent RDTSC/QPC/KUSER clocks, sane LastError) -- a \"not found\"\n  stub is a value; (2) MEASURE before reversing: run two different probes, diff every operand stream at the final compare\n  (inputs-invariant streams = stored target/masks), then ask which keys depend on input; (3) chained-block ciphers (key_j from\n  plaintext block j-1): decode block 0 from any probe, extend the probe progressively (8 -> 24 -> 38 chars; probe length must\n  equal the target's length word); (4) OR-verdicts carry decoys: enumerate every accepted group, submit only the `flag{32hex}`\n  one; (5) self-hashing `.text`: never byte-patch, hook in the emulator or shadow `.text`; (6) don't re-implement a hash you\n  only need to execute; skip deliberate slow loops instead. Speakeasy (Windows PE emulator with API/PEB/TEB stubs) saves the\n  scaffolding; never run the sample natively.\n- **Timed windows**: download dominates (D16 TT 52 s of 64 s). WASM sizes = 5-byte PADDED LEB128; PE machine map must include\n  0x8664 -> `x86-64`.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0162NLqqYNewcDT11DeSdpNN","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"231816e3-d655-4fc4-9734-2a09a078ac00","uuid":"7a893eb8-bb52-4ab7-a578-dde14e7b332c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:42:43.488Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md","content":"# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-30; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (OBSERVATIONS, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, D8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations\"): solvers derive structure, degrade per field.\n- One `evidence.zip` (AES, password `infected`), CUMULATIVE from D3: one group per past day (`dNN--sample.<ext>`, `variant-000`\n  before D22) + ONE new container/language per day: D1 C ELF, D2 C++ (ELF/MinGW PE32+), D3 .NET, D4 Go, D5 Rust, D6 Java jar,\n  D7 Kotlin jar, D8 Swift (67 MB), D9 Nim, D10 Zig, D11 D, D12 FPC, D13 Crystal, D14 ObjC, D15 C `-stripped`/`-symbolized`, D16\n  WASM `-compact`/`-direct`, D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL + `PK19` overlay, D20 Haskell + `RS20` overlay, D21 OCaml\n  `-loader.elf` + `-plugin.cmxs`, D22 F# (+ `FSharp.Core.dll`), D23 VB.NET, D24 Scala jar PAIR `-vulnerable`/`-corrected`, D25\n  Clojure jar PAIR, D26 Groovy jar (+ `crash/trace.json`), D27 V ELF PAIR `-gcc.elf`/`-tcc.elf`, D28 Odin ELF TRIO `-family-a`/\n  `-family-b`/`-false-friend`, **D29 FreeBASIC ELF PAIR `-O0.elf`/`-O3.elf` (43.9 KB each, glibc, not stripped, differ in 12\n  bytes), D30 Haxe->Neko bytecode TRIO `-loader.n`/`-library.n`/`-config.n` (~20.9 KB each, magic `NEKO`; first VM-bytecode\n  member since WASM; the D19 enum token `neko_bytecode` finally shipped)**.\n  Since D18 each day = a THEME on a new language: call graph, packing, overlays, shared libs, managed<->native bridge, anti-\n  analysis, PATCH DIFF (D24), BOUNDS ROOT CAUSE (D25), CRASH TRIAGE (D26), COMPILER ATTRIBUTION (D27), FAMILY CLUSTERING (D28),\n  **OPTIMIZATION EQUIVALENCE (D29 \"Two binaries, same source, different compiler moods ... prove they're semantically the same\n  program\"), CAMPAIGN GRAPH (D30 \"Reconstruct the loader, library, and config graph across the whole set and map the operation\n  end to end\")**. D31 is the LAST day: expect a capstone \"across the whole set\" (D30's wording already says it) and/or backfill #4.\n- Ids `dNN_artifact_sha256_K` / `dNN_analysis_<field>`; multi-member groups add `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>`. **The `<tag>` is NOT\n  always the basename token**: D21-D28 tag = basename role (`family-a` -> `family_a`), but D29 `unoptimized_`/`optimized_` route to\n  `-O0.elf`/`-O3.elf` and D30 `config_capsule_` routes to `-config.n` -- the QUESTION says \"Use the unique dNN-- member whose\n  basename ends O3.elf\": route on that sentence first, tag second. Unqualified ids = consensus of the members the question names.\n- From D2 every new member embeds the **HCFG** blob `'HCFG' | u8 ver | u8 xor_key | u16le len | u32le crc32(plain) | xor'd JSON\n  @12`; only its STORAGE changes (Variant axes). **D30 changed the MAGIC: `HGRF` (same 12-byte layout) carrying a campaign-graph\n  JSON with the config NESTED under `config`** -- scan for any `[A-Z]{4}` + this header that crc-validates, not only `HCFG`.\n- The hard part is the GM's label for `exact_text` fields; **the organizers RE-ISSUE the contract** when a label is unguessable\n  (D17 `hcfg_storage` -> enum). Since D24 EVERY question is a full SPEC (layout, scan direction, member choice, JSON path).\n- **The contract LEAKS future days**: D19 \"RS20 for Day 20\", d07 \"for Day 26 use the primary classfile\", enum `neko_bytecode`\n  (D19 -> shipped D30). All came true. After D30 no unseen token/day number remains -- re-grep the D31 contract anyway.\n- **Theme asked on its own group only sometimes**: D19/D20 yes, D21-D25 no, D26 yes (JSON sidecar), D27 no, D28/D29/D30 ONLY via\n  routing + consensus (no similarity, optimization or graph-edge id; D30 asked graph.config.* but not nodes/edges/load_order).\n  14 ids per group since D28 (sha256 per member + `<role>_format`/`<role>_machine` + 4 consensus config_* + role config_*).\n- **Every member embeds a `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` template** (unasked) whose `family` names the theme: D25\n  `clojure_bounds_root_cause_trace`, D26 `groovy_synthetic_crash_trace`, D27 `v_cross_backend_attribution_trace`, D28\n  `odin_family_cluster_trace`, D29 `freebasic_optimization_variant_trace`/`semantic_equivalence_only`; D30 puts the theme in the\n  HGRF record itself (`schema huntress.binary.campaign_graph.v1`, `effects isolated_multi_process_event_graph_only`).\n- Question count: 80 on D8, +10/day to 160, D17 204, +12/day to D27 324, D28 392 = 28 x 14 (backfill #3), **D29 406, D30 420\n  (+14/day, no new backfill)**. Mastery = `setN.` copies, +1 set/day (D28 12, D29 13 = 5278 ids, D30 14 = 5880 ids). Timed:\n  D28 TT 54 s; **D29 TT 3.0 s / M 5.7 s; D30 TT 3.1 s / M 6.1 s (all CORRECT first POST)**.\n- **Bonus flag challenge (D30 \"SHA1-Hulud\", separate slug)**: ONE `flag` answer, per-team build, 3 wrong submissions max, a\n  hardened Rust PE64 crackme (self-hashing `.text`, anti-debug, env fingerprint FED INTO THE KEYS, CBC-style two-pass cipher,\n  OR-verdict with decoys). Organizers: Day-30 only. Method is in Pitfalls (`reference/D30_SHA1HULUD_LESSONS.md` = full write-up).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, storage per container: `.hcfg` section (D2/D10/D14), .NET FieldRVA (D3), Go/Rust\n  rodata, base64 in a jar constant pool (Java/Kotlin; Scala `$` module, Clojure `<ns>__init` `encoded-config`, Groovy\n  `encodedConfig`) / Swift/Nim/D/Crystal literal, RAW FPC `.data`, WASM data seg 0, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`, D19 packed overlay,\n  D20 RS20 overlay, D21 plugin `.data`, D22 RAW twice (`.text` + PE overlay), D23 PE overlay, D27-D29 RAW appended at\n  `e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize` (file ends with the record; \"Scan backward from the end ... first CRC32-valid\"), **D30 HGRF RAW at\n  the END of each Neko `.n` (tail 0 bytes, no ELF section table to compute image_end)**. Rule: scan for `HCFG`/`SENGR...` (jars:\n  every class's constant pool) AND any record magic the question names, accept only crc32(plain) match AND parsing JSON, keep\n  scanning past failures (D9 decoys); scan in the DIRECTION the question states. Storage never changed WITHIN a day.\n- **Record magic / payload schema (D30)** -- `HGRF` = `HCFG` layout (\"byte-4 version, byte-5 XOR key, little-endian length and\n  CRC32 ... same 12-byte layout as HCFG\"); JSON = `{schema, campaign_id, nodes[], edges[\"a->b\"], load_order[], config{campaign,\n  domain, ipv4, url, mutex, windows_path, linux_path, service, host_model}, this_role, network, effects}`. The question's path\n  `graph.config.campaign` names the RECORD first: `graph` is NOT a JSON key -> drop a leading segment that is not a key and names\n  the record (graph/record/root/<magic>), then walk the dots. Consensus: \"confirm all three canonical campaign graphs match when\n  this_role is omitted\" = drop `this_role`, compare canonical JSON of all members, answer from the member named (loader.n).\n- **Overlay layout per day (D19 PK19, D20 RS20)** -- appended at image end, magic `<2 caps><day>`, header spelled by the QUESTION:\n  PK19 `magic|ver|k1|k2|pad|u32le packed_len @8|sha256 @12|packed @44`, unpack `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`; RS20 `magic|ver|u32le\n  resource_len @8|u16le scratch_len @12|sha256(scratch) @16|HCFG @48|scratch`. Rule: `rfind(magic)`, parse listed widths, verify.\n- **Location / storage as answer** -- `hcfg_offset` = decimal FILE offset (base64 -> the `S`, RAW -> the `H`); `overlay_offset`\n  = the magic, `overlay_size` = len - offset; `hcfg_resource_size` = u32le @+8. `hcfg_storage` enum in order: `base64` ->\n  `raw_hcfg_section` -> `wasm_data_segment` -> `raw_const_array` -> `raw`.\n- **Any other encoding -> `lib.binary.hcfg_scan(data)`** (hex/b32/b85/UTF-16/reversed/xor/zlib/rolling xor/custom b64/split/\n  int-array/strided/RC4/AES/TEA/ChaCha/stack-built); `hcfg_find` = first valid hit.\n- **Config VALUE SHAPES** -- crc, key and values re-roll per variant; timed modes change the SHAPE: campaign `BRNN-000` ->\n  `BRNN-<8 HEX>` (D28 false friend `FF28-`), domain `variant-000.dayNN...` (D29) / `campaign-000.day30...` (D30) ->\n  `<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid`, mutex `Global\\HuntressBRNN-000[_000]` -> `Global\\Huntress<12 HEX>`, url `.../v/BR29-000`\n  / `.../stage/BR30-000` -> `https://<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid/<word>/<10hex>`; one word pool (sync/hub/core/mesh/relay/\n  stage/edge/cache/vault/proxy/node/gate) drawn independently for domain, url host, url path. Extra keys appear without warning\n  (D28 `host_model`/`ipv4`; D30 `windows_path`/`linux_path`/`service`). Rule: copy verbatim; never regex-check a shape.\n- **Container per member** -- ELF vs PE32+ re-rolls per member in Mastery (d02, d04, d10); dispatch on MAGIC (`7f454c46`, `MZ`,\n  `PK`, `\\0asm`, `NEKO`). The format question spells the rule (\"Classify final bytes by magic and parsed container ... neko_bytecode\n  for NEKO bytecode\"). ELF-worded ids still apply to a PE re-roll (D28 TT d10: `section_count` = NumberOfSections).\n- **Member routing** -- (1) id tag = longest `[^a-z0-9]+` token naming exactly one member (multi-word: `family_a`, `false_friend`,\n  `config_capsule`); (2) the question's \"basename ends X\" / \"Use the dNN-- X member\" wins when the tag is a SEMANTIC word that is\n  not in any basename (D29 `optimized` -> `O3.elf`, `unoptimized` -> `O0.elf`, substring trap: `unoptimized` contains `optimized`;\n  D30 `config_capsule` -> `config.n`); (3) the tag can precede the field family (`corrected_config_url`) and the field can itself\n  start with `config` (`config_capsule_graph_config_campaign` = member `config.n`, field `graph.config.campaign`). `sha256_K` =\n  ARCHIVE order, never sorted. Question-named routing runs AFTER the tag peel (D21 dropped 26 ids otherwise).\n- **Unqualified id over a named subset (D24-D30)** -- \"Decode both dNN-- role members and require their config objects to be\n  byte-for-byte equal\" (D24/D25/D27/D29), D28 \"Decode family-a.elf and family-b.elf ... do not use false-friend.elf\", D30 \"Use\n  loader.n's decoded HGRF graph.config object after confirming all three ... match when this_role is omitted\": decode exactly the\n  named members, normalise as told, assert equal, answer from the named one. The excluded look-alike has its OWN valid config.\n- **Theme sidecar inside the member (D26)** -- jar entry `crash/trace.json` (`huntress.synthetic_crash.v1`, frames innermost-\n  first); entry whose name ends `trace.json`, answer frames[0]; \"every frame in the primary classfile method-name set\" = inclusion.\n- **Primary vs support members (D3, D22, D23)** -- primary assembly = the `.dll` that is not a framework/dependency (FSharp.Core,\n  System.*, Microsoft.*); hash ALL members. Basenames: `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*` since D22.\n- **Stripped carry-over d01** -- re-rolls stripped in some sets: symbols/disassembly `[]`, has_symtab `false`, recover_code `none`.\n- **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` ids (D30 14 sets), each its own delivery; each set's 1st question ends `Evidence case:\n  dNN-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]` = set->delivery map. Per-member caches key on (delivery, member name)\n  or sha256, never `id(bytes)` (D25: 5/9 sets cross-wired).\n- **kind / field sets per group** -- `elf_class`/`machine` exact_text on d01 but INTEGER on d08/d15/d21+ (dispatch on\n  `answer_format.kind`); old groups gain ids over days (D8, D17, D28): answer by field name from THAT member's facts dict.\n- **Backfill #3 spec grammar (D28, 54 ids on d01-d27)** -- public substring predicates (Latin-1 [+UTF-16LE]), regex counts over\n  NONEMPTY `.symtab` names (`.dynsym` only when no `.symtab`: d13 771 not 1255), sorted LF-join sha256 (UNIQUE names for\n  `method_names_sha256`), colon-join of member digests, Jcc byte scans in `.text`, `cli_runtime` Major.Minor, `section_count`,\n  PK19 keys, size ids w/o a named magic = the day's own overlay magic (d20 `overlay_size` = len - rfind(`RS20`)). Rule:\n  implement the sentence literally (`lib.binary.generic_field`). No backfill #4 on D29/D30.\n- **Speed flags (no answer change)** -- CPU contention: re-measure with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py`;\n  floor = inflate + sha256 of every member (all asked); D30 single solve phase 1.3 s, 14-set Mastery 1.5 s.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"AES Encrypted\" | `7z x -pinfected -y evidence.zip` (Python: `pyzipper`); `sha256sum *` for every `artifact_sha256_K` (archive order within the group) |\n| `readelf -h -S` hint, ELF header questions | `readelf -hSW`, `readelf -sW`; `readelf -p .huntress` for the custom-section `marker` (D1, re-asked D17) |\n| \"constant returned by recover_code\" / `disassembly` | `objdump -d -M intel --no-show-raw-insn` around `<recover_code>`; capstone on the FUNC symbol's bytes |\n| Stripped C build, no `.symtab` | answer the absence the question defines (`[]`/`none`); recon only: leaf `b8 imm32 c3` (`lib.binary.recover_return_constants`) |\n| C++ / \"mangled\" / \"vtable\" / \"RTTI\" | `nm -C` / `c++filt`; `_ZTV`/`_ZTI`/`_ZTS`; PE: `objdump -t file.exe` (COMDAT `.text$<mangled>`) |\n| `PE32+` MinGW `.exe` | `objdump -t` (COFF symbols), `pefile` (Machine, OPTIONAL_HEADER.Magic, sections incl. `.hcfg`) |\n| .NET (`BSJB`, `.runtimeconfig.json`; F# `FSharp.Core`, VB.NET `Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core`) | `ilspycmd` / `dnfile`; `pe_cli`/`i386`/`v4.0.30319`; PRIMARY dll only; raw `grep -abo HCFG` -> first crc-valid hit |\n| P/Invoke / \"bridge\" (`DllImportAttribute`, ModuleRef) | dnfile `md.ModuleRef`, `md.ImplMap` rows; `ilspycmd` for `[DllImport]` signatures |\n| Anti-analysis predicates (Debugger/Stopwatch/Environment TypeRefs, env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`) | NEVER run it: asked ids are header + HCFG (static); record the predicate list |\n| Go / Rust | `go version -m f`, `lib.binary.go_buildinfo`/`go_pclntab_funcs`; Rust: header + `HCFG` scan, `rustfilt` |\n| `.jar` (Java/Kotlin/Scala/Clojure/Groovy, `Created-By: Huntress deterministic <Lang> factory`) | unzip, Main-Class, `javap -v -p`; HCFG base64 `ldc` may be in Scala `Foo$`, Clojure `<ns>__init`, Groovy `encodedConfig`; `unzip -l` for NON-class sidecars |\n| Crash artifact (`crash/trace.json`, `core`, `*.dmp`, hs_err, ASan) | `jq . trace.json` (frames innermost-first); native: `readelf -n core` -> RIP -> `addr2line -f -e bin`; capstone the faulting insn |\n| Twin/role members (`-stripped`/`-symbolized`, `-loader`/`-plugin`, `-vulnerable`/`-corrected`, `-gcc`/`-tcc`, `-O0`/`-O3`) | route `<tag>_` ids (tag may be a semantic word: `optimized` = `-O3`); diff if asked: `javap -p -c` / `objdump -d` per symbol + `diff`, `rz-diff -t functions a b` |\n| N look-alikes (`-family-a`/`-family-b`/`-false-friend`) | `cmp -l A B \\| wc -l` per pair (D28 twins 1 byte, stranger ~2k), per-member HCFG (stranger `FF28-`); consensus = NAMED members only |\n| V / Odin / FreeBASIC ELF (`main__main`+`builtin__*`; `/odin/base/runtime/*.odin`; fbc rtlib `dev_scrn_init.c`/`dev_scrn_write.c` FILE syms, `fb_*`) | plain ELF (`elf`/62); HCFG RAW at image_end (`grep -abo HCFG F`), \"scan backward from the end\" |\n| **`NEKO` magic / `.n` members (D30: Haxe 4.3.7 build, strings `std/neko/*.hx`, globals `@classes`/`@Loader`/`@String`; header `NEKO` + u32le nglobals/nfields/codesize)** | format `neko_bytecode`; config record RAW at EOF: `grep -abo 'HGRF\\|HCFG' F`, rfind + crc gate; JSON path from the question (`graph.config.X` -> obj[\"config\"][\"X\"]); `nekoc`/`haxe` only for theme facts |\n| Record magic you have not seen (`HGRF`, next ???) \"uses the same 12-byte layout as HCFG\" | generic 4-byte-magic record decoder: magic\\|ver\\|key\\|u16 len\\|u32 crc\\|xor payload; scan direction + member from the question |\n| Backfill \"Evaluate this public predicate\", \"count names that match /re/\", \"sort ... SHA-256\" | `lib.binary.generic_field(blob, suffix, question, member)`; `.symtab` only (`.dynsym` if none) |\n| Same-source builds named by COMPILER or FLAGS, \"name the toolchain\", \"account for every optimization\" | header + consensus HCFG (asked D27/D29). Facts if asked: `readelf --debug-dump=info F \\| grep -m2 producer`, `.comment`, gcc IPA suffixes, tcc `.stab`, PT_INTERP libc; O-level: function count/inlining, `.text` size |\n| Swift ELF (`swift5_*`, 60+ MB) | never eager-parse symbols; regex `SENGR` base64 in `.rodata`; `bin/swift-demangle` |\n| Nim / D / Crystal / FPC / ObjC / Ada / Fortran / COBOL / Haskell / OCaml ELF | plain ELF for header ids; base64 `SENGR` (offset = the `S`) or RAW (offset = the `H`); COBOL/Haskell config in PK19/RS20 overlay; OCaml HCFG in plugin `.data` |\n| File size > `e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize` | OVERLAY: `xxd -s <image_end> F`; magic `<2 caps><day>` or bare record; parse header fields the question lists, verify hash |\n| `\\0asm` | `lib.binary.wasm_layout` / `wasm-objdump -x`; `wasm`/`wasm32`; HCFG RAW in data segment 0 |\n| `kind: enum` + rule list, or text describing bytes | the question IS the spec (D17, D19, D30): implement it literally, emit one listed token |\n| **Single `flag` answer, \"crackme\", per-team build, 3 wrong max (D30 SHA1-Hulud)** | static strings/decoders first (answer-first), then EMULATE (Speakeasy / unicorn) with a PLAUSIBLE host, hook the final compare, differential probes; see Pitfalls |\n| Packed / `UPX!` / real code reversing | `lib.binary.packer_info` -> `upx -d` on a COPY; `rizin -q -c \"aaa; pdf @ sym.<fn>\"`; Ghidra headless (last resort) |\n\n## Day by day\n**D1-D16** (one language/day): D1 C ELF headers/`.huntress`/recover_code (~14 min, 4 wrong); D2 C++ ELF/MinGW PE, first HCFG,\nPE symbols = COMDAT `.text$<mangled>`; D3 .NET `pe_cli` after ~50 synonyms (~1 h 48 min); D4 Go `amd64` REJECTED -> `x86-64`;\nD6 jar constant-pool base64; D8 Swift 67 MB + backfill #1 + integer elf_class/machine; D9 Nim raw decoys + `hcfg_offset`; D10\n`has_hcfg_section`; D12 HCFG RAW; D14 ObjC `.hcfg`; D15 stripped/symbolized `<qualifier>_` ids; D16 wasm pair `wasm`/`wasm32`.\n**D17 \"Decoder Ring\"**: Ada + backfill #2; `hcfg_storage` burned ~10.9k POSTs / 3.5 h until the contract revision (enum).\n**D18-D23** (T+11 s .. T+2:25): Fortran; GnuCOBOL + `PK19` overlay (questions spelled the stub); Haskell + `RS20`\n(`hcfg_resource_size`); OCaml loader + `.cmxs` (question-named routing AFTER the tag peel); F# + support DLL (\"FIRST record that\nvalidates\"); VB.NET PE overlay (timed modes re-shaped values).\n**D24-D27** (T+35..80 s, 0 wrong): Scala/Clojure twin jars (12-id twin template; D25 Mastery `id(bytes)` cache cross-wiring);\nGroovy + `crash/trace.json` theme ASKED; V gcc/tcc twins, RAW HCFG at image_end, \"scan backward from the end\" (zero new code).\n**D28 \"Family Resemblance\"** (392 Qs; T+3:23, 6 rejected POSTs): Odin trio, family consensus \"do not use false-friend.elf\";\nBACKFILL #3 (54 spec-worded ids) sank 4 all-or-nothing batches on d20 `overlay_size` and d13 `crystal_symbol_count`.\n\n**D29 \"Fraternal Twins\"** (406 Qs; **CORRECT T+1:20, 0 rejected**; TT 3.0 s / Mastery 13 sets 5.7 s, first POST).\n- Artifact: FreeBASIC (fbc) ELF pair `d29--sample-O0.elf`, `-O3.elf` (43,931 B each, glibc dynamic, not stripped, `crtstuff.c` +\n  fbc rtlib FILE symbols; the two differ in only 12 bytes despite the O-level names). HCFG RAW appended at EOF-387.\n- 14 new ids: 2 sha256, `unoptimized_`/`optimized_` format + machine (integer 62), 4 consensus config_* (\"Decode both d29-- role\n  members and require ... byte-for-byte equal\"), 4 `optimized_config_*`. Insight: the id tags are WORDS, the basenames carry `O0`/\n  `O3`; the question's \"basename ends O3.elf\" routed them. Theme (optimization accounting / semantic equivalence) unasked; trace\n  family `freebasic_optimization_variant_trace`. Carried-over solver banked 392, then 6 + 8 new ids.\n\n**D30 \"Campaign Trail\"** (420 Qs; **CORRECT T+1:18**, 10 rejected = the race harness's `none` placeholder probes on the d30\nconfig ids, 0 real wrong answers; TT 3.1 s / Mastery 14 sets (5880 ids) 6.1 s, first POST).\n- Artifact: Haxe 4.3.7 -> Neko bytecode trio in archive order `d30--sample-config.n`, `-library.n`, `-loader.n` (20.9 KB each,\n  `NEKO` header identical, Haxe std paths `std/neko/*.hx` leak the organizer's build dir). Each ends with a RAW `HGRF` record\n  (ver 1, xor key e.g. 0xf1, ~695 B JSON, 0 bytes after it): `huntress.binary.campaign_graph.v1` {campaign_id `DAY30-000`, nodes\n  [loader.n, library.n, config.n], edges `loader.n->library.n`, `library.n->config.n`, load_order, config{...}, this_role\n  loader/library/config, network none, effects `isolated_multi_process_event_graph_only`}; no HCFG in any member.\n- 14 new ids: 3 sha256, `loader_`/`library_`/`config_capsule_` format (`neko_bytecode`, first try), 4 consensus config_* (\"Use\n  loader.n's decoded HGRF graph.config object after confirming all three canonical campaign graphs match when this_role is\n  omitted\"), 4 `config_capsule_graph_config_*` (config.n's own record).\n- Key insight: read the record path literally but resolve `graph.` as the record name (JSON top level has `config`, no `graph`);\n  normalise by deleting `this_role` before the 3-way equality. Tools: `xxd -l 16`, `grep -abo HGRF`, a 15-line rfind+crc+xor\n  decoder; ~40 lines added to the cumulative solver (`graph_record`, `d30_graph`). Graph edges/load order NOT asked.\n- **Bonus \"SHA1-Hulud\"** (flag crackme, see header): our 4 worker launches (~1 h 45 min, 0 wrong submits) did not get the flag;\n  a reviewer's manual analysis solved it in ~5 min (CORRECT T+2:20 from release). Lost time: an emulator with \"clean = not found\"\n  env stubs ran to completion SILENTLY on every input (env answers feed the keys -> poisoned target), read as \"gate bailed\";\n  25 min modelling SHA-1 stub variants that only needed to execute; byte-at-a-time attack defeated by the backwards second pass.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n| Field family | Accepted form | Rejected (never resubmit) |\n|---|---|---|\n| elf_class | exact_text: `ELF64`/`ELF32`; `kind: integer` (D8+): `64`/`32` | ELFCLASS64; `2`/`1` |\n| machine (`kind: integer`, role members D15-D30) | decimal e_machine (`62`), also ET_DYN `.cmxs`, every compiler/O-level | — |\n| endianness | `little` / `big` | little endian, lsb, msb |\n| machine (ELF exact_text) | `x86-64`, `x86`, `AArch64`, `ARM` (D19+ text: tool labels and codes also accepted) | EM_X86_64, x86_64, amd64 |\n| machine (PE FILE_HEADER) | 0x14c -> `i386`; 0x8664 -> `x86-64` | x86 (PE i386); raw `0x8664` |\n| architecture | the same machine words (Go amd64 -> `x86-64`) | amd64, arm64, 386, x86_64 |\n| elf_type | `ET_EXEC` / `ET_DYN` | EXEC |\n| entry_point, crc32_hex, xor_key_hex | lowercase hex with `0x` (crc `0x%08x`, key `0x%02x`) | — |\n| recover_code (`kind: integer`) | base-10 integer (`mov eax, 0x1fa4` -> 8100); `none` if the symbol is absent | the stripped leaf's constant |\n| has_* | enum `true`/`false` | — |\n| marker | exact `.huntress` string without the NUL; `none` if missing | — |\n| format (enum) | `elf`, `pe`, `pe_cli`, `jar`, `wasm`, **`neko_bytecode` (D30 Haxe->Neko `.n`, CONFIRMED)** | ELF, ELF64, exe, pe32+, jar_jvm, ~50 .NET synonyms |\n| format / arch per container | compiled ELF any language/compiler/O-level `elf`/`x86-64`; WASM `wasm`/`wasm32`; .NET any language `pe_cli`/`i386`; any JVM jar `jar`; Neko `neko_bytecode` | x86 for PE i386 |\n| C++ symbols ELF / PE | bare Itanium mangled name / COMDAT section name `.text$<mangled>` | demangled; bare on PE |\n| section_names (JSON) | pyelftools order INCLUDING the leading `\"\"` | list without \"\" (pre-D17) |\n| symbols / disassembly (JSON) | non-empty .symtab names, table order, dupes kept / capstone intel `\"mov eax, 8100\"`, `\"ret\"` | hex imm, `\"ret \"` |\n| methods / access_flags / method_count (jar) | Main-Class method_info names incl. `<init>` / decimal `49` / count incl. synthetics (d26 = 10) | — |\n| crash_fault_method / crash_frames_match_methods | trace.json `frames[0]` verbatim / set inclusion `true`/`false` | — |\n| metadata_version | BSJB root string `v4.0.30319` | net8.0 / TFM |\n| config_* (HCFG) | verbatim from decoded JSON (mutex ONE backslash); consensus of the NAMED members; D19 from the unpacked overlay | JSON-escaped `\\\\`; `none` when merely hidden |\n| config_* (HGRF, D30) | `graph.config.<key>` = decoded record JSON `[\"config\"][key]` verbatim; unqualified = loader.n after this_role-less 3-way match; `config_capsule_graph_config_*` = config.n's own record | `none` placeholders (10 rejected) |\n| hcfg_version / xor_key_hex / hcfg_offset | header byte 4 decimal / byte 5 `0x%02x` / decimal FILE offset (`S` base64, `H` raw) | — |\n| overlay_offset / overlay_size / hcfg_resource_size | last occurrence of the day's magic / len - that offset / RS20 u32le @+8 | non-day magic (19) |\n| hcfg_storage (enum, D17) | `base64`, `raw_hcfg_section`, `raw_const_array`, `wasm_data_segment`, `raw` | every free-text spelling (~10.9k probes) |\n| compression_methods (jar, json) | sorted distinct ZIP method ids `[0,8]` | — |\n| backfill #3 counts / hashes / header text (D28) | `.symtab` nonempty names (`.dynsym` only if none); `section_count` = e_shnum incl. 0 (PE: NumberOfSections); sorted LF-join sha256; colon-join of member digests; `cli_runtime` `2.5`; `packing_key_1/2_hex` `0x%02x` | d13 count with `.dynsym` (1255) |\n| flag (bonus crackme, D30) | the accepted INPUT itself, `flag{<32 hex>}` (program prints \"correct, the flag is \" + input) | decoys that also print correct (`your flag is in another castle`, short `flag{nic...`) -- never submitted |\nNaming law: native format = container only; managed .NET = `pe_cli`; Java broke it (`jar`); VM bytecode = `<vm>_bytecode`.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **A synthetic label with no derivable spelling** (D3 ~1.5 h; D17 `hcfg_storage` ~10.9k POSTs): stop after ~10 single-id probes\n  plus one `hctf labels` run, write HELP.md, RE-PULL THE CONTRACT periodically and diff each id. Never mass-probe exact_text.\n- **Reversing what the question already specifies** (D19): read the longest question of each new family FIRST; size fields =\n  the exact header field the layout names. D30: the HGRF layout, scan direction and normalisation were all in the question.\n- **Absence vs hidden**: `none`/`[]`/`false` only when ABSENT (stripped d01), wrong when merely HIDDEN (D19 packed config; D30\n  race-harness `none` placeholders for the HGRF config ids -> 10 rejected probes, harmless but useless: a new record magic means\n  \"decode it\", not \"absent\").\n- **A multi-field POST is all-or-nothing** (D2, D28): POST carried-over ids first (they bank), then each NEW field family alone\n  or bisect on the first rejection; a heuristic answer to a new spec is a guess until accepted.\n- **Routing**: peel the longest multi-word member tag, but when the tag is a semantic word (`optimized`, `config_capsule`) map it\n  through the question's \"basename ends X\"; mind substring tags (`unoptimized` ⊃ `optimized`); a field that starts with `config`\n  after a role tag (`config_capsule_graph_config_url`) is still a role field. Read `answer_format.kind` per id.\n- **JSON paths in questions** (D30 `graph.config.campaign`): the first segment may name the RECORD, not a key -- resolve against\n  the decoded object, dropping a non-key leading segment; never answer `none` because `obj[\"graph\"]` is missing.\n- **\"The theme is never asked\" is NOT a rule** (D26): list every member's NON-code entries (`unzip -l`, sections, resources,\n  overlays, tail records) and parse any JSON sidecar up front. Unasked D27-D30 beyond routing; record theme facts in NOTES.md.\n- **Per-member caches keyed on `id(bytes)`** (D25 Mastery, 55 wrong ids): key on (delivery, member name) / sha256. Symptom: a\n  rejected value that is VALID for another group of the same delivery.\n- **Archives**: never unzip recursively; jar members are deflated (`grep HCFG file.jar` finds nothing) -- inflate every entry.\n  Huge members (D8 67 MB): cheap encodings first, crc-gate every hit.\n- **Decoy magics** (D9): code that checks the magic embeds `\"HCFG\"` literals; len 0 => crc32(b\"\")==0 passes. Require non-empty\n  JSON; scan DIRECTION per question (D22 first-from-start, D27-D30 backward from EOF); offsets from `re.finditer().start()`.\n- **ELF-worded id on a PE re-roll** (D28 TT d10): every ELF header/section/symbol field needs a PE mapping.\n- **Crackme with no oracle (D30 SHA1-Hulud)**: (1) SILENCE on every input under emulation = environment answers feed the keys,\n  not \"my input is wrong\": make every fingerprint report a PLAUSIBLE real host (4+ CPUs, 8 GB, 1920x1080, no hypervisor bit\n  CPUID 0x40000000, no tool processes/drivers/registry markers, coherent RDTSC/QPC/KUSER clocks, sane LastError) -- a \"not found\"\n  stub is a value; (2) MEASURE before reversing: run two different probes, diff every operand stream at the final compare\n  (inputs-invariant streams = stored target/masks), then ask which keys depend on input; (3) chained-block ciphers (key_j from\n  plaintext block j-1): decode block 0 from any probe, extend the probe progressively (8 -> 24 -> 38 chars; probe length must\n  equal the target's length word); (4) OR-verdicts carry decoys: enumerate every accepted group, submit only the `flag{32hex}`\n  one; (5) self-hashing `.text`: never byte-patch, hook in the emulator or shadow `.text`; (6) don't re-implement a hash you\n  only need to execute; skip deliberate slow loops instead. Speakeasy (Windows PE emulator with API/PEB/TEB stubs) saves the\n  scaffolding; never run the sample natively.\n- **Timed windows**: download dominates (D16 TT 52 s of 64 s). WASM sizes = 5-byte PADDED LEB128; PE machine map must include\n  0x8664 -> `x86-64`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":4,"newStart":1,"newLines":4,"lines":["-# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-28; updated after every day)","+# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-30; updated after every day)"," "," How this lane has looked so far (OBSERVATIONS, not guarantees):"," - **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, D8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations\"): solvers derive structure, degrade per field."]},{"oldStart":7,"oldLines":271,"newStart":7,"newLines":235,"lines":["   D7 Kotlin jar, D8 Swift (67 MB), D9 Nim, D10 Zig, D11 D, D12 FPC, D13 Crystal, D14 ObjC, D15 C `-stripped`/`-symbolized`, D16","   WASM `-compact`/`-direct`, D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL + `PK19` overlay, D20 Haskell + `RS20` overlay, D21 OCaml","   `-loader.elf` + `-plugin.cmxs`, D22 F# (+ `FSharp.Core.dll`), D23 VB.NET, D24 Scala jar PAIR `-vulnerable`/`-corrected`, D25","-  Clojure jar PAIR, D26 Groovy jar (+ `crash/trace.json` entry), D27 V-language ELF PAIR `-gcc.elf`/`-tcc.elf` (one V source,","-  two C backends, both musl-dynamic x86-64), **D28 Odin ELF TRIO `-family-a.elf`/`-family-b.elf`/`-false-friend.elf` (22 KB","-  glibc PIEs, stripped, same size and layout; a/b differ in ONE byte, the false friend in ~2k bytes + its own config)**.","-  Since D18 each day = a THEME on a new language: call graph (D18), packing (D19), resources/overlays (D20), shared libraries","-  (D21), managed<->native bridge (D22), anti-analysis (D23), PATCH DIFFING (D24), BOUNDS-ERROR ROOT CAUSE + reachability (D25),","-  CRASH TRIAGE (D26), COMPILER ATTRIBUTION (D27 \"name the toolchain\"), **FAMILY CLUSTERING (D28 \"These binaries might be related","-  -- or they might just look alike. Cluster them by behavior, watch out for false friends, and sort the family from the","-  strangers\")**. D24-D26 = vuln arc (3 days); D27-D28 = ATTRIBUTION arc (toolchain -> family). 3 days left: expect the arc's","-  3rd step (variant/lineage ordering, shared-code/similarity measures, YARA-style family signature) or a capstone/backfill on","-  D31. Language track: D27 V and D28 Odin = niche native languages (both predicted by the atlas). Left: Hare, Vala/Genie, C3,","-  Cython, hxcpp, Haxe->Neko (`neko_bytecode` still in the enum, unseen), Elixir/BEAM, niche JVM.","-  Ids `dNN_artifact_sha256_K` / `dNN_analysis_<field>`; multi-member groups add `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` (D15/D16/D21/D24/","-  D25/D27/D28; hyphenated roles become underscores: `family-a.elf` -> `d28_analysis_family_a_machine`, `false_friend_*`) and","-  unqualified ids whose QUESTION names the member (D21) or demands consensus of the NAMED subset (D24/D25/D27 both twins; D28","-  \"Decode family-a.elf and family-b.elf ... do not use false-friend.elf\").","+  Clojure jar PAIR, D26 Groovy jar (+ `crash/trace.json`), D27 V ELF PAIR `-gcc.elf`/`-tcc.elf`, D28 Odin ELF TRIO `-family-a`/","+  `-family-b`/`-false-friend`, **D29 FreeBASIC ELF PAIR `-O0.elf`/`-O3.elf` (43.9 KB each, glibc, not stripped, differ in 12","+  bytes), D30 Haxe->Neko bytecode TRIO `-loader.n`/`-library.n`/`-config.n` (~20.9 KB each, magic `NEKO`; first VM-bytecode","+  member since WASM; the D19 enum token `neko_bytecode` finally shipped)**.","+  Since D18 each day = a THEME on a new language: call graph, packing, overlays, shared libs, managed<->native bridge, anti-","+  analysis, PATCH DIFF (D24), BOUNDS ROOT CAUSE (D25), CRASH TRIAGE (D26), COMPILER ATTRIBUTION (D27), FAMILY CLUSTERING (D28),","+  **OPTIMIZATION EQUIVALENCE (D29 \"Two binaries, same source, different compiler moods ... prove they're semantically the same","+  program\"), CAMPAIGN GRAPH (D30 \"Reconstruct the loader, library, and config graph across the whole set and map the operation","+  end to end\")**. D31 is the LAST day: expect a capstone \"across the whole set\" (D30's wording already says it) and/or backfill #4.","+- Ids `dNN_artifact_sha256_K` / `dNN_analysis_<field>`; multi-member groups add `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>`. **The `<tag>` is NOT","+  always the basename token**: D21-D28 tag = basename role (`family-a` -> `family_a`), but D29 `unoptimized_`/`optimized_` route to","+  `-O0.elf`/`-O3.elf` and D30 `config_capsule_` routes to `-config.n` -- the QUESTION says \"Use the unique dNN-- member whose","+  basename ends O3.elf\": route on that sentence first, tag second. Unqualified ids = consensus of the members the question names."," - From D2 every new member embeds the **HCFG** blob `'HCFG' | u8 ver | u8 xor_key | u16le len | u32le crc32(plain) | xor'd JSON","-  @12`; only its STORAGE changes (see Variant axes). Scan raw bytes for `HCFG` AND base64 `SENGR...`, crc-gate every hit; when","-  both miss, look past the image end (overlay) and read the question. Parse the whole JSON dict (never-asked keys exist).","+  @12`; only its STORAGE changes (Variant axes). **D30 changed the MAGIC: `HGRF` (same 12-byte layout) carrying a campaign-graph","+  JSON with the config NESTED under `config`** -- scan for any `[A-Z]{4}` + this header that crc-validates, not only `HCFG`."," - The hard part is the GM's label for `exact_text` fields; **the organizers RE-ISSUE the contract** when a label is unguessable","-  (D17 `hcfg_storage` -> enum + ordered rules). Since D24 EVERY question is a full SPEC (sha256 \"ZIP central-directory order ...","-  member K (1-based)\", format rule list, HCFG layout + carrier rule, JAR \"Base64-alphabet UTF-8 constants >= 80 characters ...","-  first CRC32-valid\", D26 \"Parse crash/trace.json ... first string in its frames array\", D27 \"Scan backward from the end\").","-- **The contract LEAKS future days**: D19 \"RS20 for Day 20\", d07 \"for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit\" (both","-  came true). Open after D28: enum `neko_bytecode` (D22-D28 added no new token/day). Grep each contract for `[A-Z]{2}\\d\\d`, `Day NN`, unseen enum values.","-- **Theme asked on its own group only sometimes**: D19/D20 yes (overlay fields), D21-D25 NO, D26 YES (`crash_fault_method`,","-  `crash_frames_match_methods`, from a JSON SIDECAR inside the member), D27 NO (compiler fingerprints unasked), **D28 ONLY via","-  routing** (family consensus config_* + `false_friend_config_campaign`; no similarity/cluster field). 14 ids = 3 sha256 +","-  `<role>_format`/`<role>_machine` x3 + 4 family-consensus config_* + 1 false_friend config.","-- **Every member embeds a `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` template** (unasked) {branch, event_count, campaign, family","-  `<lang>_<theme>_trace`, effects, network none} gated on env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (+ `HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT` D25-D26); family","-  NAMES THE THEME: D25 `clojure_bounds_root_cause_trace`, D26 `groovy_synthetic_crash_trace` (+ `huntress.synthetic_crash.v1`","-  sidecar), D27 `v_cross_backend_attribution_trace`/`equivalent_behavior_only`, D28 `odin_family_cluster_trace`/","-  `behavior_cluster_only` + `cluster_marker_positive` (4 records per member; the false friend's event_counts differ) -- grep","-  `_trace\"` to read the day's theme.","-- Question count: 80 on D8, +10/day to 160, D17 204 (backfill #2), +12/day to D27 324, **D28 392 = 28 groups x 14 (BACKFILL #3:","-  54 new ids pad EVERY old group to 14, all spelled as specs -- public predicates, regex counts, sorted-join sha256)**. Mastery =","-  `setN.` copies, +1 set/day (**D28 12 sets = 4704 ids, ~17 MB per delivery**). Timed: D26 TT 5.3 s / M 8.2 s; D27 TT 5.4 s /","-  M 14.5 s; **D28 TT 54 s (live worker: d10 re-rolled to PE) / Mastery CORRECT first POST (solve 2.4 s, submit 4.9 s)**.","+  (D17 `hcfg_storage` -> enum). Since D24 EVERY question is a full SPEC (layout, scan direction, member choice, JSON path).","+- **The contract LEAKS future days**: D19 \"RS20 for Day 20\", d07 \"for Day 26 use the primary classfile\", enum `neko_bytecode`","+  (D19 -> shipped D30). All came true. After D30 no unseen token/day number remains -- re-grep the D31 contract anyway.","+- **Theme asked on its own group only sometimes**: D19/D20 yes, D21-D25 no, D26 yes (JSON sidecar), D27 no, D28/D29/D30 ONLY via","+  routing + consensus (no similarity, optimization or graph-edge id; D30 asked graph.config.* but not nodes/edges/load_order).","+  14 ids per group since D28 (sha256 per member + `<role>_format`/`<role>_machine` + 4 consensus config_* + role config_*).","+- **Every member embeds a `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` template** (unasked) whose `family` names the theme: D25","+  `clojure_bounds_root_cause_trace`, D26 `groovy_synthetic_crash_trace`, D27 `v_cross_backend_attribution_trace`, D28","+  `odin_family_cluster_trace`, D29 `freebasic_optimization_variant_trace`/`semantic_equivalence_only`; D30 puts the theme in the","+  HGRF record itself (`schema huntress.binary.campaign_graph.v1`, `effects isolated_multi_process_event_graph_only`).","+- Question count: 80 on D8, +10/day to 160, D17 204, +12/day to D27 324, D28 392 = 28 x 14 (backfill #3), **D29 406, D30 420","+  (+14/day, no new backfill)**. Mastery = `setN.` copies, +1 set/day (D28 12, D29 13 = 5278 ids, D30 14 = 5880 ids). Timed:","+  D28 TT 54 s; **D29 TT 3.0 s / M 5.7 s; D30 TT 3.1 s / M 6.1 s (all CORRECT first POST)**.","+- **Bonus flag challenge (D30 \"SHA1-Hulud\", separate slug)**: ONE `flag` answer, per-team build, 3 wrong submissions max, a","+  hardened Rust PE64 crackme (self-hashing `.text`, anti-debug, env fingerprint FED INTO THE KEYS, CBC-style two-pass cipher,","+  OR-verdict with decoys). Organizers: Day-30 only. Method is in Pitfalls (`reference/D30_SHA1HULUD_LESSONS.md` = full write-up)."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)"," - **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, storage per container: `.hcfg` section (D2/D10/D14), .NET FieldRVA (D3), Go/Rust","-  rodata, base64 in a jar constant pool (Java/Kotlin, D24 Scala `$` module, D25 Clojure `<ns>__init.class` `encoded-config` Var,","-  D26 Groovy `static final String encodedConfig` in the Main-Class) / Swift/Nim/D/Crystal literal, RAW FPC `.data`, WASM data seg 0, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`, D19 packed overlay, D20 RS20 overlay,","-  D21 OCaml plugin `.data`, D22 F# RAW twice (`.text` + PE overlay: \"FIRST record that validates\"), D23 VB.NET RAW PE overlay,","-  D27 V gcc+tcc RAW appended EXACTLY at `e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize` with NO day magic (the file ends with the record) and the","-  question rule reversed: \"Scan backward from the end of the member for literal HCFG magic and accept the first CRC32-valid\".","-  Rule: scan for `HCFG` and `SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*=*` (jars: every class's constant pool), accept only crc32(plain) match AND","-  parsing JSON, keep scanning past failures (D9 Nim decoys); scan in the DIRECTION the question states (D22 first-from-start,","-  D27 `rfind` loop from EOF); never a fixed offset or a fixed class. Storage never changed WITHIN a day (single/TT/all Mastery sets).","-- **Overlay layout per day (D19 PK19, D20 RS20)** -- appended at `e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize`, magic `<2 caps><day>`, header","-  spelled by the QUESTION: PK19 `magic|ver|k1|k2|pad|u32le packed_len @8|sha256(unpacked) @12|packed @44`, unpack `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`;","-  RS20 `magic|ver @4|u32le resource_len @8|u16le scratch_len @12|sha256(scratch) @16|HCFG @48 raw|scratch`. Rule: `o =","-  data.rfind(magic)` (\"final\"), parse the listed widths, verify bounds + hash; unspecified transform -> known-plaintext `HCFG`.","-- **Location / storage as answer** -- `hcfg_offset` = decimal FILE offset (base64 -> the `S`, RAW -> the `H`); `overlay_offset` =","-  the magic, `overlay_size` = len - offset; `hcfg_resource_size` = the u32le @+8 (380). `hcfg_storage` (D17 enum) in order:","-  `base64` -> `raw_hcfg_section` -> `wasm_data_segment` -> `raw_const_array` (other native data section) -> `raw`.","-- **Any other encoding -> `lib.binary.hcfg_scan(data)`** (hex/base32/85/UTF-16/reversed/xor/zlib/multibyte+rolling xor/byte maps/","-  custom b64/split/int-array/strided/RC4/AES/TEA/ChaCha/stack-built); `hcfg_find` = first valid hit. Not the PK19 stub.","-- **xor key / config VALUE SHAPES** -- crc, key byte and campaign/domain/mutex/url re-roll per variant. Timed modes change the","-  SHAPE too: D23 campaign `BRNN-00V` -> `BRNN-<8 uppercase hex>`, d01 marker `BR01-CATALOG-00V` -> `BR01-<8hex>`, d01 FILE symbol","-  `variant-000.c` -> `sample.c`; D24 also domain `node-00V.dayNN...` -> `<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid` (word: sync/hub/","-  core/mesh/relay/stage, D25-D26 also edge/cache/vault/proxy/node), mutex `Global\\HuntressBRNN_00V` -> `Global\\Huntress<12 uppercase","-  hex>`, url `.../api/BRNN-00V` -> `https://<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid/<word>/<10hex>`; D27 shows ONE word pool for","-  domain, url host and url path (sync/hub/core/mesh/relay/stage/edge/cache/vault/proxy/node/gate), each drawn independently.","-  D28 false friend: campaign prefix `FF28-` (`FF28-000` single, `FF28-<8HEX>` timed) vs the family's `BR28-`; new keys","-  `host_model` (`workstation`) and `ipv4` (TEST-NET dotted quad) are asked too.","-  Rule: copy values verbatim from the decoded JSON/symtab; never regex-check a value shape or key on `00V` indices.","-- **Container per member** -- ELF vs PE32+ re-rolls per member in Mastery (d02, d04, d10 `pe`); labels from THIS member's header;","-  dispatch on MAGIC (`7f454c46`, `MZ`, `PK`, `\\0asm`, next `NEKO`). PE symbol fields = COMDAT `.text$<mangled>`. Extensions lie","-  about role, not container (D21 `.cmxs` = ELF ET_DYN). **ELF-worded backfill ids still apply to a PE re-roll** (D28 TT d10 `.exe`:","-  \"Read ELF e_shnum ... including index 0\" -> GM took FILE_HEADER.NumberOfSections, 9, no +1): map each ELF field to its PE twin.","-- **Member qualifier in the id (D15/D16/D21/D24)** -- peel the longest field prefix that is a `[^a-z0-9]+` token of exactly one","-  member name (`stripped`/`symbolized`, `compact`/`direct`, `loader`/`plugin`, `vulnerable`/`corrected` D24+D25, `gcc`/`tcc` D27,","-  `family_a`/`family_b`/`false_friend` D28 = basename `-`->`_`, MULTI-WORD; roles can be compiler names, so never hard-code the","-  vocabulary; `family` alone names TWO members -> take the longest token naming exactly one); the token can sit","-  BEFORE the field family (D24 `d24_analysis_corrected_format`, `..._corrected_config_url`). `sha256_K` = ARCHIVE order, never","-  sorted (D24: vulnerable is member 1).","-- **Member named in the QUESTION (D21)** -- after the qualifier peel, if >1 member remains, keep the one whose basename ends with","-  the token after `basename ends` / `Use the dNN--`. ORDER MATTERS (running it first dropped 26 ids on D21).","-- **Unqualified id over a twin pair / named subset (D24, D25, D27; D28)** -- \"Decode both dNN-- role members and require their","-  config objects to be byte-for-byte equal before using the common value\"; D28 \"Decode family-a.elf and family-b.elf ...","-  common FAMILY value; do not use false-friend.elf\": decode the members the question NAMES, drop the excluded one, assert equal","-  JSON, answer the common value. The excluded look-alike carries a DIFFERENT valid config (campaign `FF28-...` vs `BR28-...`), so","-  \"first member\" or \"all members agree\" logic is wrong here -- parse the include/exclude names from the question.","-- **Theme sidecar inside the member (D26)** -- jar entry `crash/trace.json` (`huntress.synthetic_crash.v1`, `kind`, `frames`","-  innermost-first), IDENTICAL in all 12 deliveries while config re-rolled. Rule: entry whose name ends `trace.json` (never a","-  fixed path), answer frames[0] verbatim; \"every frame in the primary classfile method-name set\" = set inclusion; missing =","-  `none`/`false`. Primary classfile (d07 and d26) = the manifest Main-Class, never a `$_main_closure1`; method_count = ALL","-  method_info rows incl. Groovy synthetics (10). Inner class names keep `Variant000` although basenames say `sample`.","-- **Member basename vocabulary (D22)** -- `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`; group by `dNN--` + extension/role tag only.","-- **Primary vs support members (D3, D22, D23)** -- primary assembly + `.runtimeconfig.json` (+ D22 `FSharp.Core.dll`); question:","-  \"primary managed assembly ... runtimeconfig and dependency DLL members are delivery support only\". Primary = the `.dll` whose","-  name is not a framework/dependency (FSharp.Core, System.*, Microsoft.*), i.e. the one carrying HCFG; hash ALL members.","-- **Stripped carry-over d01** -- re-rolls stripped in some sets (D15-D17 Mastery, D17/D19 TT, D23 Mastery set6): symbols/","-  disassembly `[]`, has_symtab `false`, recover_code `none` (GM-confirmed; leaf-heuristic constants rejected). Pair by sha256.","-- **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` ids (2-12 sets; D27 11 x ~36 MB, D28 12 x ~17 MB), each its own delivery; each set's 1st question ends `Evidence","-  case: dNN-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]` (TT `dNN-tt-...`) = set->delivery map. Per-member caches key on","-  (delivery, member name) or sha256, never `id(bytes)` (D25: 5/9 sets cross-wired, see Pitfalls).","-- **kind / field sets per group** -- `elf_class`/`machine` exact_text on d01 but INTEGER (`64`/`62`) on d08/d15/d21 (dispatch on","-  `answer_format.kind`, which can change between fetches, D17); `has_<x>` = a structural marker of <x> in THIS member; old groups","-  gain ids over days (D8, D17, D28): answer by field name from THAT member's facts dict.","-- **Backfill #3 spec grammar (D28, 54 ids on d01-d27)** -- every new old-group id spells its rule: \"Evaluate this public predicate","-  ... true exactly when the final bytes [as Latin-1 or UTF-16LE] contain X [or any nonempty ELF symbol name contains Y]\"","-  (`has_nim/fpc/gnat_runtime`, `has_decoy_branch`); \"From ELF symbol-table entries with nonempty resolved names, count names that","-  match /re/\" (`d_symbol_count`, `crystal_symbol_count`, `handler_symbol_count`, `symbol_count`); \"sort ... join with one LF ...","-  SHA-256\" (`handler_symbols_sha256`, `method_names_sha256` over UNIQUE names); \"join digests with ':' ... SHA-256\"","-  (`structural_ordered_set_sha256`); byte scans (`conditional_branch_opcode_count`: 0x70-0x7f and 0f 80-8f in `.text`, one","-  left-to-right pass); header reads (`cli_runtime` = CLI header Major.Minor, `section_count`, PK19 `packing_key_1/2_hex`); new","-  config keys (`host_model`, `ipv4`); role-member config ids for the twin NOT asked before (`vulnerable_`, `symbolized_`,","-  `direct_`, `plugin_`, `gcc_`). Rule: implement the sentence literally (`lib.binary.generic_field` covers all of them); \"ELF","-  symbol-table entries\" = `.symtab` only (dupes kept), `.dynsym` ONLY when there is no `.symtab` (d13: 771 accepted, 1255 with","-  .dynsym rejected); a size id whose question names no magic = the day's own overlay magic (d20 `overlay_size` = len -","-  rfind(`RS20`) = 463; a generic `<2 caps><2 digits>` match gave 19, rejected).","-- **Speed flags (no answer change)** -- CPU contention: re-measure with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py`; D25 TT","-  solve phase 8.0 s at 300 ids under load, D26 3.2 s (TT) / 3.9 s (10-set Mastery); isolated single ~0.6-1.2 s.","+  rodata, base64 in a jar constant pool (Java/Kotlin; Scala `$` module, Clojure `<ns>__init` `encoded-config`, Groovy","+  `encodedConfig`) / Swift/Nim/D/Crystal literal, RAW FPC `.data`, WASM data seg 0, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`, D19 packed overlay,","+  D20 RS20 overlay, D21 plugin `.data`, D22 RAW twice (`.text` + PE overlay), D23 PE overlay, D27-D29 RAW appended at","+  `e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize` (file ends with the record; \"Scan backward from the end ... first CRC32-valid\"), **D30 HGRF RAW at","+  the END of each Neko `.n` (tail 0 bytes, no ELF section table to compute image_end)**. Rule: scan for `HCFG`/`SENGR...` (jars:","+  every class's constant pool) AND any record magic the question names, accept only crc32(plain) match AND parsing JSON, keep","+  scanning past failures (D9 decoys); scan in the DIRECTION the question states. Storage never changed WITHIN a day.","+- **Record magic / payload schema (D30)** -- `HGRF` = `HCFG` layout (\"byte-4 version, byte-5 XOR key, little-endian length and","+  CRC32 ... same 12-byte layout as HCFG\"); JSON = `{schema, campaign_id, nodes[], edges[\"a->b\"], load_order[], config{campaign,","+  domain, ipv4, url, mutex, windows_path, linux_path, service, host_model}, this_role, network, effects}`. The question's path","+  `graph.config.campaign` names the RECORD first: `graph` is NOT a JSON key -> drop a leading segment that is not a key and names","+  the record (graph/record/root/<magic>), then walk the dots. Consensus: \"confirm all three canonical campaign graphs match when","+  this_role is omitted\" = drop `this_role`, compare canonical JSON of all members, answer from the member named (loader.n).","+- **Overlay layout per day (D19 PK19, D20 RS20)** -- appended at image end, magic `<2 caps><day>`, header spelled by the QUESTION:","+  PK19 `magic|ver|k1|k2|pad|u32le packed_len @8|sha256 @12|packed @44`, unpack `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`; RS20 `magic|ver|u32le","+  resource_len @8|u16le scratch_len @12|sha256(scratch) @16|HCFG @48|scratch`. Rule: `rfind(magic)`, parse listed widths, verify.","+- **Location / storage as answer** -- `hcfg_offset` = decimal FILE offset (base64 -> the `S`, RAW -> the `H`); `overlay_offset`","+  = the magic, `overlay_size` = len - offset; `hcfg_resource_size` = u32le @+8. `hcfg_storage` enum in order: `base64` ->","+  `raw_hcfg_section` -> `wasm_data_segment` -> `raw_const_array` -> `raw`.","+- **Any other encoding -> `lib.binary.hcfg_scan(data)`** (hex/b32/b85/UTF-16/reversed/xor/zlib/rolling xor/custom b64/split/","+  int-array/strided/RC4/AES/TEA/ChaCha/stack-built); `hcfg_find` = first valid hit.","+- **Config VALUE SHAPES** -- crc, key and values re-roll per variant; timed modes change the SHAPE: campaign `BRNN-000` ->","+  `BRNN-<8 HEX>` (D28 false friend `FF28-`), domain `variant-000.dayNN...` (D29) / `campaign-000.day30...` (D30) ->","+  `<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid`, mutex `Global\\HuntressBRNN-000[_000]` -> `Global\\Huntress<12 HEX>`, url `.../v/BR29-000`","+  / `.../stage/BR30-000` -> `https://<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid/<word>/<10hex>`; one word pool (sync/hub/core/mesh/relay/","+  stage/edge/cache/vault/proxy/node/gate) drawn independently for domain, url host, url path. Extra keys appear without warning","+  (D28 `host_model`/`ipv4`; D30 `windows_path`/`linux_path`/`service`). Rule: copy verbatim; never regex-check a shape.","+- **Container per member** -- ELF vs PE32+ re-rolls per member in Mastery (d02, d04, d10); dispatch on MAGIC (`7f454c46`, `MZ`,","+  `PK`, `\\0asm`, `NEKO`). The format question spells the rule (\"Classify final bytes by magic and parsed container ... neko_bytecode","+  for NEKO bytecode\"). ELF-worded ids still apply to a PE re-roll (D28 TT d10: `section_count` = NumberOfSections).","+- **Member routing** -- (1) id tag = longest `[^a-z0-9]+` token naming exactly one member (multi-word: `family_a`, `false_friend`,","+  `config_capsule`); (2) the question's \"basename ends X\" / \"Use the dNN-- X member\" wins when the tag is a SEMANTIC word that is","+  not in any basename (D29 `optimized` -> `O3.elf`, `unoptimized` -> `O0.elf`, substring trap: `unoptimized` contains `optimized`;","+  D30 `config_capsule` -> `config.n`); (3) the tag can precede the field family (`corrected_config_url`) and the field can itself","+  start with `config` (`config_capsule_graph_config_campaign` = member `config.n`, field `graph.config.campaign`). `sha256_K` =","+  ARCHIVE order, never sorted. Question-named routing runs AFTER the tag peel (D21 dropped 26 ids otherwise).","+- **Unqualified id over a named subset (D24-D30)** -- \"Decode both dNN-- role members and require their config objects to be","+  byte-for-byte equal\" (D24/D25/D27/D29), D28 \"Decode family-a.elf and family-b.elf ... do not use false-friend.elf\", D30 \"Use","+  loader.n's decoded HGRF graph.config object after confirming all three ... match when this_role is omitted\": decode exactly the","+  named members, normalise as told, assert equal, answer from the named one. The excluded look-alike has its OWN valid config.","+- **Theme sidecar inside the member (D26)** -- jar entry `crash/trace.json` (`huntress.synthetic_crash.v1`, frames innermost-","+  first); entry whose name ends `trace.json`, answer frames[0]; \"every frame in the primary classfile method-name set\" = inclusion.","+- **Primary vs support members (D3, D22, D23)** -- primary assembly = the `.dll` that is not a framework/dependency (FSharp.Core,","+  System.*, Microsoft.*); hash ALL members. Basenames: `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*` since D22.","+- **Stripped carry-over d01** -- re-rolls stripped in some sets: symbols/disassembly `[]`, has_symtab `false`, recover_code `none`.","+- **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` ids (D30 14 sets), each its own delivery; each set's 1st question ends `Evidence case:","+  dNN-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]` = set->delivery map. Per-member caches key on (delivery, member name)","+  or sha256, never `id(bytes)` (D25: 5/9 sets cross-wired).","+- **kind / field sets per group** -- `elf_class`/`machine` exact_text on d01 but INTEGER on d08/d15/d21+ (dispatch on","+  `answer_format.kind`); old groups gain ids over days (D8, D17, D28): answer by field name from THAT member's facts dict.","+- **Backfill #3 spec grammar (D28, 54 ids on d01-d27)** -- public substring predicates (Latin-1 [+UTF-16LE]), regex counts over","+  NONEMPTY `.symtab` names (`.dynsym` only when no `.symtab`: d13 771 not 1255), sorted LF-join sha256 (UNIQUE names for","+  `method_names_sha256`), colon-join of member digests, Jcc byte scans in `.text`, `cli_runtime` Major.Minor, `section_count`,","+  PK19 keys, size ids w/o a named magic = the day's own overlay magic (d20 `overlay_size` = len - rfind(`RS20`)). Rule:","+  implement the sentence literally (`lib.binary.generic_field`). No backfill #4 on D29/D30.","+- **Speed flags (no answer change)** -- CPU contention: re-measure with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py`;","+  floor = inflate + sha256 of every member (all asked); D30 single solve phase 1.3 s, 14-set Mastery 1.5 s."," "," ## Recognition cues -> first move"," | You see | First move |"," |---|---|","-| `evidence.zip`, \"AES Encrypted\" | `7z x -pinfected -y evidence.zip` (Python: `pyzipper`); `sha256sum *` for every `artifact_sha256_K` (K = archive order within the group) |","+| `evidence.zip`, \"AES Encrypted\" | `7z x -pinfected -y evidence.zip` (Python: `pyzipper`); `sha256sum *` for every `artifact_sha256_K` (archive order within the group) |"," | `readelf -h -S` hint, ELF header questions | `readelf -hSW`, `readelf -sW`; `readelf -p .huntress` for the custom-section `marker` (D1, re-asked D17) |","-| \"constant returned by recover_code\" / `disassembly` | `objdump -d -M intel --no-show-raw-insn` around `<recover_code>`; capstone on the FUNC symbol's st_value..st_size bytes |","-| Stripped C build, no `.symtab` | answer the absence the question defines (`[]`/`none`); only as recon find the leaf `b8 imm32 c3` (`lib.binary.recover_return_constants`) |","-| C++ / \"mangled\" / \"vtable\" / \"RTTI\" | `nm -C` / `c++filt`; `_ZTV`/`_ZTI`/`_ZTS`; `score` method `_ZNK<len><Class>5scoreEPKc`; PE: `objdump -t file.exe` (COMDAT names) |","-| `PE32+` MinGW `.exe` | `objdump -t` (COFF symbols + string table), `pefile` (Machine, OPTIONAL_HEADER.Magic, sections incl. `