{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZdGAWKrU9Ze8Udsa42a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018Q7V6Qdv8iswKwjpHSaTWB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\nt=open(p).read()\nm=re.search(r'```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',t,re.S)\ng=json.loads(m.group(1))\nby={x['id']:x for x in g}\n# drop today's concept (seen day30, already built)\ng=[x for x in g if x['id']!='neko-bytecode-member']\nby=by\n# re-rank\nprio={'backfill-spec-grammar-extensions':1,'theme-backfill-d18-d28-fields':1,'behavior-profile-from-trace-templates':1,\n      'toolchain-attribution-verdicts':1,'family-cluster-similarity-facts':2,'false-friend-discriminator':2,\n      'fuzzy-hash-fields':2,'yara-rule-match-facts':2,'odin-language-facts':2,'hare-vala-c3-member-fixtures':2}\nfor x in g:\n    if x['id'] in prio: x['priority']=prio[x['id']]\nby['theme-backfill-d18-d28-fields']['detail']+=\" D29/D30 extend the list (same id, scope now D18-D30): d29 O0/O3 facts (function counts, .text sizes, byte-diff count, equal HCFG/trace profile = semantic_equivalence verdict, trace family freebasic_optimization_variant_trace); d30 HGRF graph facts (nodes, edges, load_order, node/edge counts, this_role per member, campaign_id, effects) -- a D31 capstone/backfill #4 is the last chance for these, so expose them as generic_field candidates.\"\nby['backfill-spec-grammar-extensions']['detail']+=\" D29/D30 added no backfill (+14 ids/day only); D31 is the last day, so backfill #4 (or a capstone) is most likely THERE: keep generic_field reading any sentence over any group incl. the d29 FreeBASIC pair and the d30 Neko trio (Neko: no ELF symtab/sections -> predicates over raw bytes, record fields over the HGRF JSON).\"\nby['family-cluster-similarity-facts']['detail']+=\" D29 (O0/O3 twins differing in 12 bytes) and D30 (3 Neko members) did not ask metrics either; keep for a D31 capstone, priority 2.\"\nby['contract-forward-hints']['detail']+=\" UPDATE D30: `neko_bytecode` (enum since D19) came true on D30 (11-day lead). The D30 contract names only past days (19/20/26) and no unseen token; the only new magic (`HGRF`) appeared without a prior leak. Keep grepping on D31 for new enum values / record magics.\"\nby['hare-vala-c3-member-fixtures']['detail']+=\" D29 FreeBASIC and D30 Haxe->Neko were the latest picks (still 'one new language per day'); D31 may add one more (Hare/C3/Vala/HashLink/hxcpp/Gleam/Pony). Header ids + tail-record scan are what matter; the language itself never changed a label.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"campaign-graph-record-facts\",\"concept\":\"Generic HCFG-layout record with ANY 4-char magic (D30 `HGRF`) + campaign-graph JSON facts: nodes, edges, load_order, this_role, nested config; dotted JSON-path resolver where the first segment may name the record\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D30 Neko trio (loader.n/library.n/config.n) each END with a RAW `HGRF` record: magic|u8 ver|u8 xor key|u16le len|u32le crc32(plain)|xor'd JSON @12 (identical to HCFG), JSON = huntress.binary.campaign_graph.v1 {campaign_id, nodes[], edges['a->b'], load_order[], config{campaign, domain, ipv4, url, mutex, windows_path, linux_path, service, host_model}, this_role, network, effects}. Asked: `graph.config.<key>` (the JSON top level has NO `graph` key -- the segment names the record) per member and as consensus 'after confirming all three canonical campaign graphs match when this_role is omitted'. Build lib.binary.record_scan(data, magic=None, direction='backward') -> [(off, magic, ver, key, obj)] accepting any [A-Z0-9]{4} magic whose header crc-validates non-empty JSON; json_path(obj, 'graph.config.campaign', record_names=('graph','record','root',magic.lower())); graph_facts(obj) -> node_count, edge_count, edges sorted/joined, load_order joined, roots/leaves, first/last node, this_role, effects; consensus_without(objs, drop_keys) -> canonical JSON equality. Register generic_field rules for ids like `graph_node_count`, `graph_edges`, `load_order`, `<role>_this_role`, `graph_edges_sha256` (LF/comma joins per the sentence). Fixtures: the three d30 members from challenges/day30/binary-campaign-trail cases + a synthetic record with a different magic and a decoy record with bad crc before it.\"},\n {\"id\":\"cross-group-campaign-correlation\",\"concept\":\"Capstone questions across the WHOLE evidence set: configs/campaigns shared between groups, counts of distinct campaigns/domains/mutexes, which groups' members agree, ordered or sorted joins + sha256 over every group's decoded config\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D30 prompt: 'Reconstruct the loader, library, and config graph across the whole set and map the operation end to end' -- the D31 finale is likely a capstone over all 30-31 groups. The cumulative solver already decodes every group's HCFG/HGRF config per member; expose a set-level facts dict: per group the consensus config (or per member when they differ, e.g. d28 false friend FF28-), distinct campaign count, groups sharing a campaign/domain word/url path word, members with NO config (role members like the d21 loader), ordered list of campaigns by day, sha256 of LF/colon joins as the sentence specifies, member count per container format (elf/pe/pe_cli/jar/wasm/neko_bytecode). Parse the question for the group range ('d01-- through d30--', 'every group', 'all members') and the join rule. Fixture: the D30 single case (420 ids) -> compute all facts and assert they are stable vs. the confirmed per-group configs.\"},\n {\"id\":\"optimization-equivalence-facts\",\"concept\":\"Optimization-level twin facts (D29 theme, unasked): O-level per member, function count / inlined functions, .text/.rodata size and sha256, byte-diff count and first differing offset, normalised-instruction hash per function, 'semantically equivalent' verdict from equal config + equal trace profile\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D29 'Fraternal Twins': FreeBASIC d29--sample-O0.elf / -O3.elf (43,931 B each, not stripped, differ in 12 bytes; ids tag them `unoptimized_`/`optimized_`; trace family freebasic_optimization_variant_trace / semantic_equivalence_only, 4 records each). Prompt: 'Diff the variants, account for every optimization, and prove they're semantically the same program.' Build lib.binary.opt_twin_facts(a, b) -> {diff_bytes, first_diff_offset, diff_sections:[...], func_count_a/b, funcs_only_in_a/b (inlined away), text_size_a/b, text_sha256_equal, same_config, same_trace_profile, semantically_equivalent}, plus opt_level_guess(blob) from DWARF producer flags (`-O3`), function-count ratio, presence of vector insns (xmm/ymm packed ops) and loop unrolling. Expose via register_generic for `<role>_function_count`, `<role>_text_size`, `diff_byte_count`, `semantically_equivalent`. Fixtures: the d29 pair from challenges/day29/binary-fraternal-twins cases + gcc -O0/-O3 builds of one C file.\"},\n {\"id\":\"semantic-role-tag-router\",\"concept\":\"Map an id's role tag to a member when the tag is a WORD absent from the basenames (D29 `optimized`->`-O3.elf`, `unoptimized`->`-O0.elf`; D30 `config_capsule`->`-config.n`), incl. substring traps (`unoptimized` contains `optimized`)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"The D29/D30 solvers routed through the question sentence ('Use the unique dNN-- member whose basename ends O3.elf'); make it a lib helper so any lane/day gets it: lib.binary.route_member(answer_id, question, members) -> member: (1) the question's 'basename ends X' / 'Use the dNN-- X member' / 'Use X's decoded ...' wins; (2) else longest tag token naming exactly one basename ('-'->'_'); (3) else an alias table (optimized/release/O2/O3, unoptimized/debug/O0, capsule/config, stub/loader, payload/plugin) only when unambiguous; tags matched as WHOLE `_`-tokens so `unoptimized` never matches `optimized`. Regression: every <tag>_ id of the D30 single contract (420 ids) resolves to the GM-confirmed member.\"},\n {\"id\":\"neko-bytecode-deep-facts\",\"concept\":\"Neko `.n` facts for a d30 backfill: header u32 nglobals/nfields/codesize, globals table (strings, floats, functions, debug info), field names, Haxe class names (`@classes`, `@Loader`, `@String`), embedded `std/neko/*.hx` source paths, Haxe version\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D30 members: 'NEKO' + u32le (214, 171, 9391) identical across loader/library/config; Haxe 4.3.7 build path strings. A capstone/backfill could ask has_haxe_runtime (substring predicate), global_count, field_count, code_size, string-global count/sha256, the HGRF offset. Extend the BUILT neko parser (lib.binary) with these fields + generic_field rules; keep it pure-Python (neko/haxe apt packages optional). Fixture: the three d30 members.\"},\n {\"id\":\"freebasic-language-facts\",\"concept\":\"FreeBASIC (fbc) identity facts for a d29 backfill: has_freebasic_runtime predicate (rtlib FILE syms dev_scrn_*.c, `fb_` symbols, `FreeBASIC` strings), fbc version, rtlib symbol counts, O-level\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D29 pair: glibc dynamic, not stripped, FILE symbols from the fbc rtlib (`dev_scrn_init.c`, `dev_scrn_write.c`), `crtstuff.c`. Mirror the D28 backfill grammar (has_<lang>_runtime public predicate, '<lang>_symbol_count' regex count over nonempty .symtab names) for FreeBASIC and register the field family; also add `fb_` cues to language_of(). Fixture: d29 members (single case).\"},\n {\"id\":\"env-keyed-crackme-emulation\",\"concept\":\"Flag crackmes whose environment fingerprint feeds the keys (D30 bonus SHA1-Hulud): plausible-host emulation profile, differential operand capture at the final compare, progressive chosen-plaintext decoding, decoy filtering\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"Organizers said this class is Day-30 only; keep the METHOD (reference/D30_SHA1HULUD_LESSONS.md): silence on every input = poisoned keys, not a failed gate; spoof a realistic host (4+ CPUs, 8 GB, 1920x1080, no CPUID hypervisor bit, no tool processes/drivers/registry markers, coherent RDTSC/QPC/KUSER clocks, sane LastError/VirtualAlloc errors); hook the compare (emulator code hook, never patch self-hashed .text), diff operand streams across two probes, decode block 0 then extend; enumerate every OR-accepted group and submit only the flag-shaped one (3 wrong max). Tool candidate: Speakeasy (Mandiant) for PE API/PEB/TEB stubs.\"},\n]\ng.extend(new)\nassert len({x['id'] for x in g})==len(g)\nbody='[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+'\\n]'\nt=t[:m.start(1)]+body+t[m.end(1):]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\n# verify\nimport subprocess\ns=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\ndone={k.split(':',1)[1] for k,v in s.items() if k.startswith('binary-reverse-engineering:') and (v.get('ok') or v.get('attempts',0)>=2)}\ng2=json.loads(re.search(r'```json\\n(.*?)\\n```',open(p).read(),re.S).group(1))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g2 if x['action']=='prebuild' and x['id'] not in done]\nprint(len(g2),'pending prebuild:',len(pend)); print(pend)\nprint(sorted(set(k for x in g2 for k in x)))\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2145,"cache_read_input_tokens":155095,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2145},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"231816e3-d655-4fc4-9734-2a09a078ac00","uuid":"718843dc-01f4-418e-81a7-d6a4fe67f0a3","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:45:08.394Z","request_id":"req_011CgZdGAJfkknQmohGa53dy","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018Q7V6Qdv8iswKwjpHSaTWB":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; py