c (`HGRF`) appeared without a prior leak. Keep grepping on D31 for new enum values / record magics.\"\nby['hare-vala-c3-member-fixtures']['detail']+=\" D29 FreeBASIC and D30 Haxe->Neko were the latest picks (still 'one new language per day'); D31 may add one more (Hare/C3/Vala/HashLink/hxcpp/Gleam/Pony). Header ids + tail-record scan are what matter; the language itself never changed a label.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"campaign-graph-record-facts\",\"concept\":\"Generic HCFG-layout record with ANY 4-char magic (D30 `HGRF`) + campaign-graph JSON facts: nodes, edges, load_order, this_role, nested config; dotted JSON-path resolver where the first segment may name the record\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D30 Neko trio (loader.n/library.n/config.n) each END with a RAW `HGRF` record: magic|u8 ver|u8 xor key|u16le len|u32le crc32(plain)|xor'd JSON @12 (identical to HCFG), JSON = huntress.binary.campaign_graph.v1 {campaign_id, nodes[], edges['a->b'], load_order[], config{campaign, domain, ipv4, url, mutex, windows_path, linux_path, service, host_model}, this_role, network, effects}. Asked: `graph.config.<key>` (the JSON top level has NO `graph` key -- the segment names the record) per member and as consensus 'after confirming all three canonical campaign graphs match when this_role is omitted'. Build lib.binary.record_scan(data, magic=None, direction='backward') -> [(off, magic, ver, key, obj)] accepting any [A-Z0-9]{4} magic whose header crc-validates non-empty JSON; json_path(obj, 'graph.config.campaign', record_names=('graph','record','root',magic.lower())); graph_facts(obj) -> node_count, edge_count, edges sorted/joined, load_order joined, roots/leaves, first/last node, this_role, effects; consensus_without(objs, drop_keys) -> canonical JSON equality. Register generic_field rules for ids like `graph_node_count`, `graph_edges`, `load_order`, `<role>_this_role`, `graph_edges_sha256` (LF/comma joins per the sentence). Fixtures: the three d30 members from 